msgid "What this guide is about"
msgstr "O čemu govori ovaj vodič"

msgid ""
"Dog behavior is not random. It is a structured system of signals, reactions,"
" and learned responses. Understanding behavior means learning how dogs "
"interpret the world, how they communicate stress or comfort, and why they "
"react in certain ways."
msgstr ""
"Ponašanje psa nije nasumično. To je strukturisan sistem signala, reakcija i "
"naučenih odgovora. Razumeti ponašanje znači naučiti kako psi tumače svet, "
"kako komuniciraju stres ili smirenost i zašto reaguju na određeni način."

msgid ""
"This guide focuses on interpretation of behavior, not training methods or "
"commands. The goal is to understand what the dog is expressing rather than "
"how to change it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Basic principles of dog communication"
msgstr "Osnovni principi pseće komunikacije"

msgid ""
"Dogs communicate primarily through body language rather than vocalization. "
"Posture, tail position, ear movement, and facial tension all carry meaning."
msgstr ""
"Psi komuniciraju prvenstveno govorom tela, a ne oglašavanjem. Položaj tela, "
"položaj repa, pokreti ušiju i napetost lica — sve to nosi značenje."

msgid ""
"Unlike humans, dogs rarely exaggerate signals. Their communication is subtle"
" and often requires context to interpret correctly."
msgstr ""
"Za razliku od ljudi, psi retko preteruju u signalima. Njihova komunikacija "
"je suptilna i često zahteva kontekst da bi se ispravno protumačila."

msgid ""
"The same behavior can mean different things depending on environment, past "
"experience, and emotional state."
msgstr ""
"Isto ponašanje može značiti različite stvari u zavisnosti od okruženja, "
"prethodnog iskustva i emotivnog stanja."

msgid "Stress and emotional signals"
msgstr "Stres i emotivni signali"

msgid ""
"Stress in dogs is often visible long before it becomes severe. Common "
"signals include lip licking, yawning, turning away, or avoiding eye contact."
msgstr ""
"Stres kod pasa često je vidljiv mnogo pre nego što postane ozbiljan. "
"Uobičajeni signali uključuju oblizivanje usana, zevaanje, okretanje glave "
"ili izbegavanje kontakta očima."

msgid ""
"These behaviors are not «bad habits» but communication attempts. They "
"indicate discomfort in a situation, even if the dog appears calm externally."
msgstr ""
"Ova ponašanja nisu «loše navike» već pokušaji komunikacije. Oni ukazuju na "
"nelagodu u situaciji, čak i ako pas spolja deluje smireno."

msgid ""
"Ignoring early stress signals can lead to escalation, such as barking, "
"freezing, or defensive reactions."
msgstr ""
"Ignorisanje ranih znakova stresa može dovesti do eskalacije — lajanja, "
"ukočenosti ili odbrambenih reakcija."

msgid "Confidence vs insecurity"
msgstr "Samopouzdanje naspram nesigurnosti"

msgid ""
"A confident dog typically shows relaxed posture, steady movement, and "
"controlled curiosity toward new environments."
msgstr ""
"Samouveren pas obično pokazuje opušten stav, stabilne pokrete i kontrolisanu"
" radoznalost prema novom okruženju."

msgid ""
"An insecure dog may hesitate, stay close to the owner, or avoid unfamiliar "
"objects and sounds. These reactions are not fixed personality traits but "
"situational responses."
msgstr ""
"Nesiguran pas može oklevati, ostajati blizu vlasnika ili izbegavati "
"nepoznate predmete i zvuke. Te reakcije nisu fiksne crte ličnosti, već "
"situacioni odgovori."

msgid ""
"Understanding the difference helps prevent misinterpretation of behavior as "
"stubbornness or disobedience."
msgstr ""
"Razumevanje razlike pomaže da se ponašanje ne protumači pogrešno kao "
"tvrdoglavost ili neposlušnost."

msgid "Social behavior and interaction"
msgstr "Društveno ponašanje i interakcija"

msgid ""
"Dog-to-dog interaction follows a structured set of signals used to establish"
" boundaries and intentions. This includes approach speed, body orientation, "
"and play initiation signals."
msgstr ""
"Interakcija između pasa prati strukturisan skup signala za uspostavljanje "
"granica i namera. To uključuje brzinu prilaska, orijentaciju tela i signale "
"za započinjanje igre."

msgid ""
"Not all dogs are equally social. Some prefer direct interaction, while "
"others require distance and gradual introduction."
msgstr ""
"Nisu svi psi podjednako društveni. Neki preferiraju direktnu interakciju, "
"dok drugima treba distanca i postepeno upoznavanje."

msgid ""
"Misreading social signals can lead to unnecessary tension between dogs, even"
" in non-aggressive situations."
msgstr ""
"Pogrešno čitanje društvenih signala može dovesti do nepotrebne napetosti "
"među psima, čak i u neagresivnim situacijama."

msgid "Common misunderstandings of behavior"
msgstr "Česta pogrešna tumačenja ponašanja"

msgid ""
"Many behaviors are incorrectly interpreted from a human perspective. For "
"example, a dog that avoids eye contact is not necessarily guilty or "
"submissive—it may simply be showing respect or avoiding conflict."
msgstr ""
"Mnoga ponašanja se pogrešno tumače iz ljudske perspektive. Na primer, pas "
"koji izbegava kontakt očima nije nužno kriv ili pokoran — on možda samo "
"iskazuje poštovanje ili izbegava sukob."

msgid ""
"Barking is another commonly misunderstood signal. It can indicate "
"excitement, alertness, fear, or communication rather than aggression."
msgstr ""
"Lajanje je još jedan često pogrešno shvaćen signal. Ono može ukazivati na "
"uzbuđenje, oprez, strah ili pokušaj komunikacije, a ne na agresiju."

msgid ""
"Correct interpretation always depends on context rather than isolated "
"actions."
msgstr ""
"Ispravno tumačenje uvek zavisi od konteksta, a ne od izolovanih postupaka."

msgid "Human influence on behavior"
msgstr "Uticaj čoveka na ponašanje"

msgid ""
"Dog behavior is shaped significantly by environment and human response. "
"Consistency, emotional tone, and household structure all influence how a dog"
" reacts over time."
msgstr ""
"Na ponašanje psa značajno utiču okruženje i reakcije ljudi. Doslednost, "
"emotivni ton i struktura domaćinstva utiču na to kako pas reaguje tokom "
"vremena."

msgid ""
"Dogs learn patterns from repetition. If a behavior is consistently "
"reinforced or ignored, it becomes part of their natural response system."
msgstr ""
"Psi uče obrasce kroz ponavljanje. Ako se neko ponašanje dosledno nagrađuje "
"ili ignoriše, ono postaje deo njihovog prirodnog sistema reakcija."

msgid ""
"This is why behavior is not fixed—it evolves based on interaction with the "
"environment."
msgstr ""
"Zato ponašanje nije fiksno — ono se razvija kroz interakciju sa okruženjem."

msgid "Reading body language: a practical reference"
msgstr "Čitanje jezika tela: praktični pregled"

msgid ""
"Tail position summarizes overall tension. A low or tucked tail signals fear "
"or shutdown, a high and stiff tail signals high arousal or a challenge, and "
"a loose, swinging tail at mid-height usually means a relaxed social mood. "
"The speed of wagging matters far less than its height and stiffness."
msgstr ""
"Položaj repa sažima ukupnu napetost. Nizak ili zavučen rep signalizuje strah"
" ili povlačenje, visok i ukočen rep signalizuje visoko uzbuđenje ili izazov,"
" a opušten, ljuljajući rep na srednjoj visini obično znači opušteno "
"raspoloženje. Brzina mašenja je daleko manje važna od visine i ukočenosti "
"repa."

msgid ""
"Ears, eyes and muzzle complete the picture. Ears pinned back can mean "
"anxiety or appeasement; wide eyes showing the whites (often called whale "
"eye) signal stress; a soft open mouth with a loose face is neutral, while a "
"closed tense muzzle is not."
msgstr ""
"Uši, oči i njuška dopunjavaju sliku. Prislonjene uši mogu značiti "
"anksioznost ili umirivanje; širom otvorene oči sa vidljivim belancem (često "
"zvano «kitovo oko») signalizuju stres; mek, otvoren sa opuštenom njuškom je "
"neutralan, dok zatvorena, napeta njuška nije."

msgid ""
"The whole body gives the strongest signal. A curved, wiggly body is "
"friendly; a stiff forward-leaning body with weight on the front legs is "
"alert or confrontational. Shaking off as if wet, especially right after a "
"stressful event, is a common way dogs release tension."
msgstr ""
"Najjači signal daje celo telo. Zakrivljeno, talasasto telo je prijateljsko; "
"ukočeno telo nagnuto unapred sa težinom na prednjim nogama je oprezno ili "
"konfrontativno. Trešenje kao da je mokro, naročito odmah nakon stresnog "
"događaja, uobičajen je način da psi oslobode napetost."

msgid "Reading signals in clusters"
msgstr "Čitanje signala u grupama"

msgid ""
"No single signal is reliable on its own. Dogs display clusters: lip licking "
"together with turning away and a lowered body clearly indicates stress, even"
" though each sign alone could mean something else entirely."
msgstr ""
"Nijedan signal nije pouzdan sam po sebi. Psi pokazuju grupe: lizanje usana "
"zajedno sa okretanjem i spuštenim telom jasno ukazuje na stres, iako bi "
"svaki znak pojedinačno mogao značiti sasvim nešto drugo."

msgid ""
"Context narrows the interpretation. The same yawning can mean simple "
"tiredness at home and tension in a veterinary clinic. Combine body language "
"with the environment, recent events, and the dog's overall state before "
"drawing conclusions."
msgstr ""
"Kontekst sužava tumačenje. Istijevanje može kod kuće značiti običan umor, a "
"u veterinarskoj ambulanti napetost. Pre nego što zaključite, povežite jezik "
"tela sa okruženjem, nedavnim događajima i ukupnim stanjem psa."

msgid "What stress looks like in everyday life"
msgstr "Kako stres izgleda u svakodnevnom životu"

msgid ""
"Early stress is easy to miss: the dog licks its lips when nobody offered "
"food, yawns repeatedly, scratches itself out of context, shakes its body, or"
" moves its head away from a hand reaching over it. These are polite requests"
" to slow down or stop."
msgstr ""
"Rani stres je lako promašiti: pas se lizne usane iako niko nije nudio hranu,"
" više puta zijeva, češe se bez povoda, trese telo ili odglavi glavu od ruke "
"koja mu se približava odozgo. To su pristojni zahtevi da se uspori ili "
"stane."

msgid ""
"If these requests are ignored, the dog may escalate to barking, jumping, "
"freezing in place, or showing teeth. This is not stubbornness — it is the "
"predictable result of earlier, quieter signals being missed."
msgstr ""
"Ako se ovi zahtevi ignorišu, pas može preći na ljanje, skakanje, zamrzavanje"
" na mestu ili pokazivanje zuba. To nije tvrdoglavost — to je predvidiv ishod"
" ranije promašenih, tiših signala."

msgid ""
"The practical response is simple: increase distance from whatever caused the"
" stress, lower your own activity level, and let the dog choose to re-"
"approach. Constant anxious-tone petting can unintentionally reinforce the "
"anxious state — calm distance helps more."
msgstr ""
"Praktičan odgovor je jednostavan: uvećajte udaljenost od onoga što je "
"izazvalo stres, spustite sopstveni nivo aktivnosti i pustite psa da sam "
"izabere kada će se ponovo približiti. Stalno mazanje u anksioznom tonu "
"nenamerno može ojačati anksiozno stanje — mirna udaljenost više pomaže."

msgid "Growling, freezing and snapping"
msgstr "Režanje, zamrzavanje i ugriz"

msgid ""
"Growling is communication, not defiance. It appears when earlier quieter "
"signals were missed, and it tells you clearly what the dog wants: distance "
"from a person, another dog, or a situation."
msgstr ""
"Režanje je komunikacija, ne prkos. Pojavljuje se kada su raniji tiši signali"
" promašeni i jasno vam govori čega pas želi: udaljenosti od osobe, drugog "
"psa ili situacije."

msgid ""
"Punishing a growl removes the warning but not the reason — the next time the"
" dog may skip straight to snapping. The reliable fix is to remove the cause "
"of discomfort, not the signal."
msgstr ""
"Kazna za režanje uklanja upozorenje, ali ne i razlog — sledeći put pas može "
"odmah preći na ugriz. Pouzdano rešenje je ukloniti uzrok nelagode, a ne "
"signal."

msgid ""
"A freeze — the dog stops moving, goes still and silent — is a higher-"
"intensity signal than a growl and deserves the same respect. After any bite "
"or attempted bite, a veterinary pain check is a sensible first step."
msgstr ""
"Zamrzavanje — pas prestane da se kreće, ćuti i ostaje nepomičan — signal je "
"jačeg intenziteta od režanja i zaslužuje isto poštovanje. Posle svakog "
"ugriza ili pokušaja ugriza, veterinarski pregled bola je pametan prvi korak."

msgid "Leash reactivity and barrier frustration"
msgstr "Reaktivnost na povodcu i frustracija od barijere"

msgid ""
"A dog that barks and lunges at other dogs on a leash is often not "
"aggressive. The leash prevents normal greeting behaviour, and frustration "
"plus high excitement comes out as barking."
msgstr ""
"Pas koji laje i juri na druge pse na povodcu često nije agresivan. Povodac "
"sprečava normalno pozdravljanje, a frustracija plus jako uzbuđenje izbija "
"kao ljanje."

msgid ""
"Distance is the working tool: the further the dog is from the trigger, the "
"more thinking it can do. Practising calm behaviour at a comfortable distance"
" teaches far more than forcing close encounters."
msgstr ""
"Udaljenost je radni alat: što je pas dalje od okidača, više može da "
"razmišlja. Vežbanje mirnog ponašanja na udobnoj udaljenosti uči daleko više "
"nego nametanje bliskih susreta."

msgid "An observation log"
msgstr "Dnevnik posmatranja"

msgid ""
"A simple diary helps more than memory. Write down three things each time: "
"what happened right before the behaviour, what the dog did, and what "
"followed. After a few entries, patterns usually become visible."
msgstr ""
"Jednostavan dnevnik pomaže više od sećanja. Svaki put zapišite tri stvari: "
"šta se dogodilo neposredno pre ponašanja, šta je pas učinio i šta je "
"usledilo. Posle nekoliko zapisa, obrasci obično postaju vidljivi."

msgid ""
"Such a record also makes it much easier to describe the problem precisely to"
" a trainer or a veterinarian later on."
msgstr ""
"Takav zapis takođe mnogo olakšava da kasnije tačno opišete problem treneru "
"ili veterinaru."

msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr "Zaključak"

msgid ""
"Understanding dog behavior is primarily about interpretation rather than "
"control. When signals are read correctly, it becomes easier to understand "
"needs, emotions, and reactions without misjudgment."
msgstr ""
"Razumevanje ponašanja psa prvenstveno je pitanje tumačenja, a ne kontrole. "
"Kada se signali ispravno čitaju, lakše je razumeti potrebe, emocije i "
"reakcije bez pogrešnih procena."

msgid ""
"This creates a more stable and predictable relationship between dog and "
"owner based on awareness rather than assumption."
msgstr ""
"To stvara stabilniji i predvidljiviji odnos između psa i vlasnika, zasnovan "
"na svesti, a ne na pretpostavkama."

