msgid "The FCI sorts dogs first of all by <strong>the work they were bred for</strong>. Sheepdogs herded flocks, hounds followed a trail, pointers helped hunt birds — the nature of this work shaped their build, coat and behaviour."
msgstr "FCI deli pse pre svega prema <strong>poslu za koji su uzgajani</strong>. Ovčari su čuvali stada, goniči su išli tragom, ptičari su pomagali u lovu na ptice — osobenosti tog posla oblikovale su njihovu građu, dlaku i ponašanje."

msgid "Each group is divided into <strong>sections</strong> that refine the purpose, origin or traits of the breeds. Some sections are further divided into breeds with and without a working trial, as well as into subsections. We do not separate the latter in our classification."
msgstr "Svaka grupa se deli na <strong>sekcije</strong> koje preciziraju namenu, poreklo ili osobine rasa. Neke sekcije se dodatno dele na rase sa radnim ispitom i bez njega, kao i na podsekcije. Njih u našoj klasifikaciji ne izdvajamo."

msgid "Each recognized breed has an official standard, prepared by its country of origin and approved by the FCI, as well as its own number."
msgstr "Svaka priznata rasa ima zvanični standard, koji priprema zemlja porekla, a potvrđuje FCI, kao i sopstveni broj."

