msgid ""
"Choosing a dog is a decision about long-term compatibility rather than "
"appearance or impulse. The right choice depends on how well a dog’s needs "
"align with your lifestyle, energy level, and living environment."
msgstr ""
"Izbor psa je odluka o dugoročnoj kompatibilnosti, a ne o izgledu ili "
"trenutnom impulsu. Pravi izbor zavisi od toga koliko se potrebe psa "
"poklapaju sa vašim životnim stilom, nivoom energije i životnim okruženjem."

msgid "Where will your companion come from?"
msgstr "Odakle će doći vaš ljubimac?"

msgid ""
"Our website is purely informational and is about dog breeds. We deliberately"
" do not recommend specific places or ways of getting a pet, because every "
"happy story of a dog joining a family has its own path."
msgstr ""
"Naš sajt je isključivo informativan i posvećen je rasama pasa. Namerno ne "
"preporučujemo konkretna mesta ni načine nabavke ljubimca, jer svaka srećna "
"priča o psu koji dolazi u porodicu ima svoj put."

msgid ""
"None of these paths is the only right one for everyone. The path you choose "
"will become part of your own story."
msgstr ""
"Nijedan od ovih puteva nije jedini ispravan za sve. Put koji vi izaberete "
"postaće deo vaše priče."

msgid ""
"Whichever way you choose, please treat the choice of the people and the "
"place you get your dog from with responsibility. Make sure that its well-"
"being, health and future come first."
msgstr ""
"Bez obzira na to koji način izaberete, odgovorno pristupite izboru ljudi i "
"mesta od kojih uzimate psa. Uverite se da su njegova dobrobit, zdravlje i "
"budućnost na prvom mestu."

msgid "Lifestyle compatibility"
msgstr "Kompatibilnost sa životnim stilom"

msgid ""
"The most important factor in choosing a dog is daily lifestyle. Time "
"availability, activity level, work schedule, and home environment all "
"influence suitability."
msgstr ""
"Najvažniji faktor pri izboru psa je svakodnevni životni stil. Raspoloživo "
"vreme, nivo aktivnosti, radni raspored i kućno okruženje utiču na "
"prikladnost."

msgid ""
"Active individuals may struggle with low-energy dogs, while calm lifestyles "
"may not meet the needs of highly energetic breeds. Mismatch often leads to "
"long-term frustration for both owner and dog."
msgstr ""
"Aktivne osobe mogu imati problem sa psima niske energije, dok miran životni "
"stil možda ne zadovoljava potrebe veoma energičnih rasa. Nepoklapanje često "
"dovodi do dugoročne frustracije i vlasnika i psa."

msgid "The goal is balance, not preference alone."
msgstr "Cilj je ravnoteža, a ne samo sklonost."

msgid "Experience level of the owner"
msgstr "Nivo iskustva vlasnika"

msgid ""
"Some dogs require more structured handling, patience, and consistency than "
"others. First-time owners often benefit from more stable and adaptable "
"breeds."
msgstr ""
"Nekim psima je potrebno više strukturisanog pristupa, strpljenja i "
"doslednosti nego drugima. Onima koji prvi put uzimaju psa često odgovaraju "
"stabilnije i prilagodljivije rase."

msgid ""
"More independent or strong-willed dogs may require prior experience and "
"clearer leadership consistency."
msgstr ""
"Nezavisniji psi ili psi sa jakom voljom mogu zahtevati prethodno iskustvo i "
"jasniju doslednost u vođenju."

msgid ""
"Matching experience level with dog temperament reduces behavioral and "
"adaptation issues."
msgstr ""
"Usklađivanje nivoa iskustva sa temperamentom psa smanjuje probleme u "
"ponašanju i adaptaciji."

msgid "Living space and environment"
msgstr "Životni prostor i okruženje"

msgid ""
"Living conditions play a major role in suitability. Apartment living, "
"suburban homes, and rural environments create very different needs for space"
" and activity."
msgstr ""
"Uslovi stanovanja igraju veliku ulogu u prikladnosti. Život u stanu, "
"prigradska kuća i ruralno okruženje stvaraju veoma različite potrebe za "
"prostorom i aktivnošću."

msgid ""
"Larger or high-energy dogs typically require more space and outdoor access, "
"while smaller or calmer breeds can adapt more easily to compact "
"environments."
msgstr ""
"Većim ili energičnijim psima obično je potrebno više prostora i pristupa "
"otvorenom, dok se manje ili smirenije rase lakše prilagođavaju manjim "
"sredinama."

msgid "Time and responsibility expectations"
msgstr "Vreme i očekivanja u vezi sa odgovornošću"

msgid ""
"Dogs require daily attention for many years. This includes routine care, "
"time presence, and consistent involvement in their daily life."
msgstr ""
"Psi zahtevaju svakodnevnu pažnju tokom mnogo godina. To uključuje redovnu "
"negu, prisustvo i dosledno učešće u njihovom svakodnevnom životu."

msgid ""
"Underestimating time requirements is one of the most common reasons for poor"
" adaptation after adoption."
msgstr ""
"Potcenjivanje vremenskih zahteva jedan je od najčešćih razloga loše "
"adaptacije nakon udomljavanja."

msgid "Questions to ask yourself first"
msgstr "Pitanja koja prvo treba da sebi postavite"

msgid ""
"Before looking at breeds, answer these questions honestly: — How many hours "
"a day will the dog realistically be alone on a normal workday? — Who will "
"walk and feed the dog during holidays, illness, or travel? — Can you absorb "
"an unexpected veterinary bill tomorrow? — Are any household members "
"allergic, afraid of dogs, or unwilling to share space? — How much physical "
"activity can you genuinely offer every day, in any weather?"
msgstr ""
"Pre nego što pogledate rase, iskreno odgovorite na ova pitanja: — Koliko "
"sati dnevno će pas realno biti sam u uobičajenom radnom danu? — Ko će psa "
"šetati i hraniti tokom praznika, bolesti ili putovanja? — Možete li podneti "
"neočekivan veterinarski račun sutra? — Da li je neko u domaćinstvu "
"alergičan, boji se pasa ili ne želi da deli prostor? — Koliko fizičke "
"aktivnosti zaista možete da ponudite svaki dan, u svakom vremenu?"

msgid ""
"The answers define your candidate group of breeds much more accurately than "
"any photo or advertisement. An active herding breed and a calm companion dog"
" can live in the same apartment — but only one of them will be happy with "
"your actual schedule."
msgstr ""
"Odgovori definišu vašu grupu rasa kandidata daleko tačnije od bilo kakve "
"fotografije ili oglasa. Aktivna pastirska rasa i miran prateći pas mogu "
"živeti u istom stanu — ali će samo jedan od njih biti srećan sa vašim "
"stvarnim rasporedom."

msgid "Puppy or adult dog"
msgstr "Štene ili odrasli pas"

msgid ""
"A puppy gives you influence over every habit but demands the most time: "
"house training, socialization, night rest, and constant supervision for the "
"first months. Expect interrupted sleep and limited freedom for the first "
"year."
msgstr ""
"Štene vam daje uticaj na svaku naviku, ali traži najviše vremena: "
"navikavanje na kuću, socijalizaciju, noćni odmor i stalni nadzor prvih "
"meseci. Očekujte prekinut san i ograničenu slobodu prve godine."

msgid ""
"An adult dog comes with an established character, usually calmer and already"
" house-trained. Adaptation takes a few weeks to a few months, but you see "
"what you are getting: energy level, attitude to people, and size."
msgstr ""
"Odrasli pas dolazi sa utvrđenim karakterom, obično mirniji i već naučen na "
"kuću. Navikavanje traje od nekoliko nedelja do nekoliko meseci, ali vidite "
"šta dobijate: nivo energije, odnos prema ljudima i veličinu."

msgid "What owning a dog costs"
msgstr "Koliko košta držanje psa"

msgid ""
"Budget beyond the purchase price: — food and treats; — regular veterinary "
"care: vaccinations, parasite prevention, annual check-ups; — insurance or a "
"dedicated emergency fund; — grooming, especially in long-haired breeds; — "
"equipment: collar or harness, leash, bed, bowls, transport box; — boarding "
"or a sitter when you travel; — training or classes in the first year."
msgstr ""
"Budžet pored kupovne cene: — hrana i poslastice; — redovna veterinarska "
"nega: vakcinacije, prevencija parazita, godišnji pregledi; — osiguranje ili "
"poseban fond za hitne slučajeve; — nega dlake, naročito kod dugodlakih rasa;"
" — oprema: ogrlica ili pojas, povodac, ležaljke, činije, transportni boks; —"
" čuvanje ili dadilja kada putujete; — obuka ili časovi prve godine."

msgid ""
"Large breeds, long-haired breeds, and brachycephalic breeds tend to cost "
"noticeably more over a lifetime. It is better to calculate a rough monthly "
"figure before choosing than to discover it after."
msgstr ""
"Velike rase, dugodlake rase i brahicefalne rase obično koštaju primetno više"
" tokom života. Bolje je pre izbora izračunati otprilike mesečni iznos nego "
"ga otkriti nakon toga."

msgid "Breed-specific checks"
msgstr "Provere specifične za rasu"

msgid ""
"For any breed you consider, look up four things in advance: predispositions "
"in the breed's health profile, the real adult size, the typical activity "
"level, and how the coat needs to be maintained. These four facts predict "
"daily life with the dog better than general descriptions of character."
msgstr ""
"Za bilo koju rasu koju razmatrate, unapred potražite četiri stvari: "
"predispozicije u zdravstvenom profilu rase, stvarna veličina odraslog psa, "
"tipičan nivo aktivnosti i kako treba održavati dlaku. Ova četiri fakta "
"predviđaju svakodnevni život sa psom bolje od opštih opisa karaktera."

msgid ""
"If you are choosing between several breeds, compare them on paper: hours "
"alone, required activity, grooming time, and common health risks. The «feel»"
" of a choice made this way stays stable much longer than the first emotional"
" impression."
msgstr ""
"Ako birate između nekoliko rasa, uporedite ih na papiru: sati provedeni "
"sami, potrebna aktivnost, vreme za negu i uobičajeni zdravstveni rizici. "
"«Osećaj» ovako donetog izbora ostaje stabilan mnogo duže od prvog "
"emocionalnog utiska."

msgid ""
"Choosing a dog is a structured decision based on compatibility, not "
"preference alone. When lifestyle, experience, and environment are aligned "
"with the dog’s needs, long-term stability becomes significantly easier to "
"achieve."
msgstr ""
"Izbor psa je strukturisana odluka zasnovana na kompatibilnosti, a ne samo na"
" sklonosti. Kada su životni stil, iskustvo i okruženje usklađeni sa "
"potrebama psa, dugoročna stabilnost se postiže znatno lakše."

msgid "Contact"
msgstr "Kontakt"

msgid "Thank you for helping improve this project"
msgstr "Hvala što pomažete da unapredimo ovaj projekat"

msgid ""
"By clicking «Send» button, you allow WoofDogs to process your information in"
" accordance with our"
msgstr ""
"Klikom na dugme «Pošalji» dozvoljavate WoofDogs-u da obradi vaše informacije"
" u skladu sa našom"

msgid "Send a message"
msgstr "Pošalji poruku"

msgid "Send"
msgstr "Pošalji"

msgid "Feel free to reach out with any questions, suggestions, or feedback."
msgstr "Slobodno nas kontaktirajte sa pitanjima, predlozima ili utiscima."

msgid ""
"<span class=\"accent-strong\">Photography credits:</span> Every photograph "
"on the website matters to us. If you are the author of a photograph and "
"would like it to be removed, or if you would like your authorship to be "
"corrected or credited differently — <span class=\"accent-strong\">please "
"write to us</span>. We are always happy to give credit where it is due."
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"accent-strong\">Zasluge za fotografije:</span> Svaka "
"fotografija na sajtu nam je važna. Ako ste autor fotografije i želite da "
"bude uklonjena, ili ako želite da autorstvo bude ispravljeno ili drugačije "
"navedeno — <span class=\"accent-strong\">pišite nam</span>. Uvek nam je "
"drago da navedemo zasluge tamo gde pripadaju."

msgid "Also:"
msgstr "Takođe:"

msgid ""
"If you notice any inaccuracies in breed descriptions, characteristics, or "
"data."
msgstr ""
"Ako primetite netačnosti u opisima rasa, karakteristikama ili podacima."

msgid ""
"If you would like to suggest a dog breed that is not yet listed on the "
"website."
msgstr "Ako želite da predložite rasu pasa koja još nije na sajtu."

msgid "If you have ideas or suggestions to improve the content or structure."
msgstr "Ako imate ideje ili predloge za poboljšanje sadržaja ili strukture."

msgid ""
"Please include a link or any relevant details to help process your request."
msgstr ""
"Molimo vas da priložite link ili relevantne detalje koji će pomoći obradi "
"vašeg zahteva."

msgid "Your feedback helps keep the information accurate and reliable."
msgstr ""
"Vaše povratne informacije pomažu da informacije ostanu tačne i pouzdane."

msgid "Thank you. Message has been sent."
msgstr "Hvala. Poruka je poslata."

msgid "Please try again later."
msgstr "Pokušajte ponovo kasnije."

