msgid "What this guide covers"
msgstr "Šta pokriva ovaj vodič"

msgid ""
"Feeding is one of the most important parts of everyday dog care. This guide "
"explains general feeding principles that apply to any healthy dog: food "
"formats, portions, feeding by age and a proper drinking regime."
msgstr ""
"Ishrana je jedan od najvažnijih delova svakodnevne nege psa. Ovaj vodič "
"objašnjava opšte principe ishrane koji važe za svakog zdravog psa: formate "
"hrane, porcije, ishranu po uzrastu i pravilan režim pijenja."

msgid ""
"This guide deliberately avoids brand names. Every dog is different: the "
"final ration always depends on age, size, activity level and health "
"condition."
msgstr ""
"Ovaj vodič namerno ne pominje brendove. Svaki pas je drugačiji: konačni "
"obrok uvek zavisi od uzrasta, veličine, nivoa aktivnosti i zdravstvenog "
"stanja."

msgid "Dry and wet food"
msgstr "Suva i mokra hrana"

msgid ""
"Dry food is convenient: it is easy to store, measure and dose. It stays "
"fresh longer, and its crunchy texture helps clean teeth mechanically."
msgstr ""
"Suva hrana je praktična: lako se čuva, meri i dozira. Duže ostaje sveža, a "
"njena hrskava tekstura pomaže mehaničkom čišćenju zuba."

msgid ""
"Wet food contains much more moisture, which helps maintain water balance. It"
" is often more palatable, which suits picky eaters, older dogs and dogs with"
" dental problems."
msgstr ""
"Mokra hrana sadrži znatno više vlage, što pomaže održavanju ravnoteže vode. "
"Često je ukusnija, pa odgovara izbirljivim psima, starijim psima i psima sa "
"problemima sa zubima."

msgid ""
"Both formats can be combined. What matters most is that the ration is "
"complete and balanced for the dog's age and size. An opened tin of wet food "
"must be stored in the refrigerator and used within a short time."
msgstr ""
"Oba formata mogu se kombinovati. Najvažnije je da obrok bude kompletan i "
"uravnotežen za uzrast i veličinu psa. Otvorenu konzervu mokre hrane treba "
"čuvati u frižideru i potrošiti u kratkom roku."

msgid "How to choose food"
msgstr "Kako odabrati hranu"

msgid ""
"Read the composition: good food lists a specific source of protein first — "
"chicken, beef or fish — instead of vague mixtures."
msgstr ""
"Pročitajte sastav: dobra hrana na prvom mestu navodi konkretan izvor "
"proteina — piletinu, govedinu ili ribu — umesto nejasnih mešavina."

msgid ""
"Consider the age category, the size of the kibble for small breeds, and "
"special needs such as allergies or sensitive digestion."
msgstr ""
"Uzmite u obzir uzrasnu kategoriju, veličinu granula za male rase i posebne "
"potrebe kao što su alergije ili osetljivo varenje."

msgid ""
"Avoid products with unclear composition, excess salt, sugar or artificial "
"colours. If in doubt, ask your veterinarian."
msgstr ""
"Izbegavajte proizvode sa nejasnim sastavom, viškom soli, šećera ili "
"veštačkih boja. Ako ste u nedoumici, pitajte svog veterinara."

msgid "Feeding across ages"
msgstr "Ishrana kroz uzraste"

msgid ""
"Puppies need small frequent meals: roughly three to four times a day, "
"gradually reduced to two meals by the age of six to twelve months."
msgstr ""
"Štenci treba da jedu manje obroke češće: otprilike tri do četiri puta "
"dnevno, a do uzrasta od šest do dvanaest meseci postepeno preći na dva "
"obroka."

msgid ""
"Adult dogs usually feel best with one or two regular meals a day at the same"
" time."
msgstr ""
"Odrasli psi se obično najbolje osećaju uz jedan ili dva redovna obroka "
"dnevno u isto vreme."

msgid ""
"Senior dogs may need smaller portions, easier-to-digest food and, often, "
"more frequent feeding. During pregnancy and lactation the dog needs more "
"food and more frequent meals."
msgstr ""
"Starijim psima možda trebaju manje porcije, lakše svarljiva hrana i, često, "
"češće hranjenje. Tokom trudnoće i laktacije psu je potrebno više hrane i "
"češćih obroka."

msgid "Portions and schedule"
msgstr "Porcije i raspored"

msgid ""
"The portion depends on weight, activity and the food itself. Use the feeding"
" table on the package as a starting point and adjust it by observing the "
"dog's condition."
msgstr ""
"Porcija zavisi od težine, aktivnosti i same hrane. Koristite tabelu ishrane "
"na pakovanju kao polaznu tačku i prilagodite je posmatranjem stanja psa."

msgid ""
"Regular meals at fixed times help digestion and prevent begging. For adult "
"dogs avoid free access to the bowl all day — it often leads to obesity."
msgstr ""
"Redovni obroci u isto vreme pomažu varenju i sprečavaju prose. Kod odraslih "
"pasa izbegavajte slobodan pristup činiji tokom celog dana — to često dovodi "
"do gojaznosti."

msgid "Treats should make up no more than ten percent of the daily calories."
msgstr "Poslastice ne smeju činiti više od deset procenata dnevnih kalorija."

msgid "Drinking regime"
msgstr "Režim pijenja"

msgid "Fresh water must be available at all times, not only during meals."
msgstr "Sveža voda mora biti dostupna u svakom trenutku, ne samo uz obroke."

msgid ""
"Change the water daily and wash the bowl regularly. In hot weather, after "
"activity or when eating dry food, the dog drinks noticeably more."
msgstr ""
"Menjajte vodu svakodnevno i redovno perite činiju. Po vrućem vremenu, nakon "
"aktivnosti ili kada jede suvu hranu, pas pije primetno više."

msgid ""
"A sudden increase or decrease in thirst can be a sign of health problems — "
"in that case, consult a veterinarian."
msgstr ""
"Nagli porast ili pad žeđi može biti znak zdravstvenih problema — u tom "
"slučaju se posavetujte sa veterinarom."

msgid "Switching food"
msgstr "Promena hrane"

msgid ""
"Change the food gradually, over seven to ten days, mixing the new food into "
"the old one in increasing proportions."
msgstr ""
"Menjajte hranu postepeno, tokom sedam do deset dana, mešajući novu hranu u "
"staru u sve većim razmerama."

msgid ""
"A sudden change often causes digestive upset: loose stool, refusal of food "
"or bloating. Watch your dog carefully during the transition."
msgstr ""
"Nagla promena često izaziva probleme s varenjem: retku stolicu, odbijanje "
"hrane ili nadimanje. Pažljivo pratite psa tokom prelaska."

msgid "Foods to avoid"
msgstr "Hrana koju treba izbegavati"

msgid ""
"Some human foods are dangerous for dogs: chocolate, grapes and raisins, "
"onions and garlic, xylitol, alcohol and cooked bones."
msgstr ""
"Neke ljudske namirnice su opasne za pse: čokolada, grožđe i suvo grožđe, luk"
" i beli luk, ksilitol, alkohol i kuvane kosti."

msgid ""
"Salty, spicy and fatty food from the table is also best avoided. Keep these "
"products out of the dog's reach."
msgstr ""
"Slanu, ljutu i masnu hranu sa stola takođe je najbolje izbegavati. Držite "
"ove proizvode van domašaja psa."

msgid "How to read the label"
msgstr "Kako čitati deklaraciju"

msgid ""
"Look at the protein and fat percentages and compare them with the dog's "
"activity. An active working dog needs more calories than a house dog of the "
"same weight — the same food can be perfect for one and too rich for the "
"other."
msgstr ""
"Gledajte procenat proteina i masti i uporedite ih sa aktivnošću psa. Aktivan"
" radni pas treba više kalorija od kućnog psa iste težine — ista hrana može "
"biti savršena za jednog, a previše bogata za drugog."

msgid ""
"The first ingredient should be a named meat source, not a vague «cereal» or "
"«meat by-products». Additives worth knowing: glucosamine and chondroitin for"
" joint support in large breeds, omega fatty acids for the coat, and no "
"unnecessary colourings."
msgstr ""
"Prvi sastojak treba da bude imenovani izvor mesa, a ne neodređeno «žito» ili"
" «mesni proizvodi». Dodaci vredni pažnje: glukozamin i hondroitin za podršku"
" zglobova kod velikih rasa, omega masne kiseline za dlaku i bez nepotrebnih "
"boja."

msgid "Homemade food: what to know"
msgstr "Domaća hrana: šta treba znati"

msgid ""
"A homemade ration is possible but must be formulated, not improvised. Plain "
"meat with rice long-term causes calcium and trace-element deficiencies; dogs"
" need a balance of protein, fat, carbohydrates, calcium, and vitamins in "
"correct proportions."
msgstr ""
"Domaća racija je moguća, ali mora biti formulisana, ne improvizovana. Obično"
" meso sa rižom dugoročno uzrokuje nedostatak kalcijuma i elemenata u "
"tragovima; psima je potrebna ravnoteža proteina, masti, ugljenih hidrata, "
"kalcijuma i vitamina u pravilnim proporcijama."

msgid ""
"If you go this route, work with a veterinarian or a pet nutrition "
"specialist: they will calculate the ration for your dog's weight, age, and "
"activity, and it makes sense to supplement it with a proven mineral premix."
msgstr ""
"Ako krenete tim putem, radite sa veterinarom ili stručnjakom za ishranu "
"životinja: izračunaće raciju prema težini, uzrastu i aktivnosti vašeg psa, a"
" ima smisla je dopuniti proverenom mineralnom mešavinom."

msgid "Safe treats and snacks"
msgstr "Sigurne poslastice i grickalice"

msgid ""
"Simple unseasoned treats are the safest: small pieces of boiled chicken or "
"turkey, lean beef, hard cheese in tiny amounts, carrot or apple slices "
"without seeds, and special dental chews given as part of the daily ration, "
"not in addition to it."
msgstr ""
"Jednostavne nezačinjene poslastice su najbezbednije: mali komadi kuvane "
"piletine ili ćuretine, nemasna govedina, tvrdi sir u malim količinama, "
"kriške šargarepe ili jabuke bez koštica i posebni dentalni zalogaji koji se "
"daju kao deo dnevne racije, a ne uz nju."

msgid ""
"Commercial treats vary hugely in calories — read the packaging and count "
"treats into the daily ration. One large biscuit can equal a quarter of a "
"small dog's daily energy need."
msgstr ""
"Komercijalne poslastice se enormno razlikuju u kalorijama — pročitajte "
"pakovanje i uračunajte poslastice u dnevnu raciju. Jedan veliki keks može "
"biti četvrtina dnevnih energetskih potreba malog psa."

msgid "Where and how to feed"
msgstr "Gde i kako hraniti"

msgid ""
"Choose a quiet corner away from the front door and the household's main "
"route, with a non-slip mat under the bowls. In a multi-dog household, feed "
"dogs separately — competition over food is a common and completely avoidable"
" source of conflict."
msgstr ""
"Izaberite miran ugao daleko od ulaznih vrata i glavnog prolaza u "
"domaćinstvu, sa prostirkom protiv klizanja ispod činija. U domaćinstvu sa "
"više pasa hranite ih odvojeno — takmičenje za hranu je česta i potpuno "
"izbeživa izvor sukoba."

msgid ""
"For tall breeds, a raised feeder reduces strain on the neck and joints; for "
"deep-chested dogs, discuss the height with your veterinarian. Slow-feeder "
"bowls and puzzle feeders turn a thirty-second gulp into five minutes of work"
" and reduce the risk of bloating."
msgstr ""
"Za visoke rase postolje za činije smanjuje napor na vrat i zglobove; za pse "
"sa dubokim grudima visinu dogovorite sa veterinarom. Činije protiv brzog "
"gutanja i slagalice pretvaraju tridesetosekundno gutanje u pet minuta rada i"
" smanjuju rizik od nadutosti."

msgid "Keeping a healthy weight"
msgstr "Održavanje zdrave težine"

msgid ""
"Check the body condition monthly: the ribs should be easy to feel with light"
" pressure but not visible, and the belly should tuck upward when viewed from"
" the side. If the ribs disappear, cut the daily portion by about ten percent"
" and add sniffing-based activity."
msgstr ""
"Proveravajte kondiciju tela mesečno: rebra treba da se lako napipaju uz blag"
" pritisak, ali ne i da se vide, a stomak da se uvlači nagore kad se gleda sa"
" strane. Ako rebra nestanu, smanjite dnevnu porciju za oko deset odsto i "
"dodajte aktivnost zasnovanu na njuškanju."

msgid ""
"Weigh food with a kitchen scale rather than a scoop — «one cup» can differ "
"by thirty percent between products and shapes. Keep a note of the daily "
"grammage on the food container so every member of the household feeds the "
"same amount."
msgstr ""
"Merite hranu kuhinjskom vagom, a ne šoljicom — «jedna šoljica» može da se "
"razlikuje za trideset odsto između proizvoda i oblika. Zapišite dnevnu "
"količinu u gramima na posudi za hranu da bi svi u domaćinstvu hranili "
"jednako."

msgid "Feeding while travelling"
msgstr "Hranjenje na putovanjima"

msgid ""
"On trips, keep the usual food and schedule: pack several days' worth in "
"sealed containers and bring the dog's own water where possible. On travel "
"days, offer a smaller meal and avoid feeding right before or immediately "
"after long exercise."
msgstr ""
"Na putovanjima zadržite uobičajenu hranu i raspored: spakujte zalihe za "
"nekoliko dana u zatvorene posude i gde je moguće ponesite pseću vodu. Na "
"dane putovanja ponudite manji obrok i izbegavajte hranjenje neposredno pre "
"ili posle duge aktivnosti."

msgid ""
"In hot weather or on active holiday days, the dog may eat less than usual — "
"this is normal if it lasts a day. Refusal of food for more than twenty-four "
"hours, or vomiting, is a reason to contact a veterinarian."
msgstr ""
"U vrućim danima ili na aktivnim praznicima pas može jesti manje nego obično "
"— to je normalno ako traje jedan dan. Odbijanje hrane duže od dvadeset "
"četiri sata ili povraćanje razlog su da kontaktirate veterinara."

msgid ""
"Feeding is a routine, but a conscious one: a stable schedule, a quality "
"ration and constant access to water are the foundation of health."
msgstr ""
"Ishrana je rutina, ali svesna: stabilan raspored, kvalitetan obrok i stalan "
"pristup vodi temelj su zdravlja."

msgid ""
"If you are not sure about the right food for your dog, always consult a "
"specialist — the right choice is easier to make together."
msgstr ""
"Ako niste sigurni koja hrana odgovara vašem psu, uvek se posavetujte sa "
"stručnjakom — pravi izbor se lakše donosi zajedno."

msgid ""
"Play is not just fun — it is a necessary part of everyday life for a dog. "
"Games give physical activity, mental load and emotional contact with the "
"owner."
msgstr ""
"Igra nije samo zabava — to je neophodan deo svakodnevnog života psa. Igre "
"pružaju fizičku aktivnost, mentalno opterećenje i emotivni kontakt sa "
"vlasnikom."

msgid ""
"This guide describes safe games that suit most dogs, from puppies to "
"seniors, and explains their benefits."
msgstr ""
"Ovaj vodič opisuje bezbedne igre koje odgovaraju većini pasa, od štenaca do "
"starijih pasa, i objašnjava njihove koristi."

msgid "Why play matters"
msgstr "Zašto je igra važna"

msgid ""
"Regular games help release excess energy, reduce stress and prevent "
"destructive behavior."
msgstr ""
"Redovne igre pomažu da se oslobodi višak energije, smanji stres i spreči "
"destruktivno ponašanje."

msgid ""
"A tired and satisfied dog sleeps better, trains better and stays calmer when"
" left alone."
msgstr ""
"Umoran i zadovoljan pas bolje spava, bolje uči i smireniji je kada ostane "
"sam."

msgid ""
"Play also strengthens the bond between you: the dog learns to trust and "
"cooperate."
msgstr "Igra takođe jača vezu između vas: pas uči da veruje i sarađuje."

msgid "Fetch and chase games"
msgstr "Igre donošenja i jurnjave"

msgid ""
"Fetch is one of the simplest games: throw a toy or a soft dummy and teach "
"the dog to bring it back. Use special toys — sticks are dangerous."
msgstr ""
"Donošenje (fetch) jedna je od najjednostavnijih igara: bacite igračku ili "
"mekanu vabicu i naučite psa da je vrati. Koristite posebne igračke — štapovi"
" su opasni."

msgid ""
"Keep sessions short, end the game at the peak of interest, and always check "
"the playing area for hazards."
msgstr ""
"Držite sesije kratkim, završite igru na vrhuncu interesovanja i uvek "
"proverite prostor za igru."

msgid ""
"For dogs that love running, games of hide-and-seek with toys and light "
"chasing work well too."
msgstr ""
"Za pse koji vole trčanje, dobro funkcionišu i igre skrivanja sa igračkama i "
"lagana jurnjava."

msgid "Tug games"
msgstr "Igre potezanja"

msgid ""
"Tug-of-war is a natural game that trains muscles and self-control. Agree on "
"the rules in advance: the game starts and ends on your command."
msgstr ""
"Potezanje je prirodna igra koja vežba mišiće i samokontrolu. Dogovorite "
"pravila unapred: igra počinje i završava se na vašu komandu."

msgid ""
"Use a special toy with a firm grip, do not pull sharply, and give the dog "
"breaks to rest."
msgstr ""
"Koristite posebnu igračku sa čvrstim hvatom, ne povlačite naglo i pravite "
"pauze za odmor."

msgid ""
"For puppies and young dogs, watch the teeth and joints — the game should not"
" turn into a fight."
msgstr ""
"Kod štenaca i mladih pasa pazite na zube i zglobove — igra ne sme prerasti u"
" borbu."

msgid "Scent games"
msgstr "Igre mirisom"

msgid ""
"Dogs perceive the world through their nose. Scent games are the best mental "
"load: hide treats or toys around the house and let the dog find them."
msgstr ""
"Psi svet doživljavaju nosom. Igre mirisom najbolje su mentalno opterećenje: "
"sakrijte poslastice ili igračke po kući i pustite psa da ih pronađe."

msgid ""
"Start with simple hiding places in the same room and gradually make the task"
" harder."
msgstr ""
"Počnite sa jednostavnim skrovištima u istoj prostoriji i postepeno "
"otežavajte zadatak."

msgid ""
"A «sniffing walk» is also a game: on part of the route, let the dog stop and"
" explore smells freely instead of walking in a straight line."
msgstr ""
"«Šetnja njušenja» je takođe igra: na delu rute pustite psa da slobodno staje"
" i istražuje mirise, umesto da hoda pravolinijski."

msgid "Puzzle toys and slow feeders"
msgstr "Slagalice i spore činije"

msgid ""
"Puzzle toys and slow feeding bowls turn eating into a small game and slow "
"down fast eaters."
msgstr ""
"Slagalice i spore činije pretvaraju hranjenje u malu igru i usporavaju brze "
"jedače."

msgid ""
"They are especially useful for smart breeds that get bored quickly, and for "
"dogs that swallow food too fast."
msgstr ""
"Posebno su korisne za pametne rase koje se brzo dosade i za pse koji gutaju "
"hranu prebrzo."

msgid "Rotate the toys regularly so they do not become boring."
msgstr "Redovno menjajte igračke kako ne bi dosadile."

msgid "Learning through play"
msgstr "Učenje kroz igru"

msgid ""
"Games are a great way to train: teach new commands in a playful format with "
"short sessions of five to ten minutes."
msgstr ""
"Igre su odličan način za obuku: učite nove komande u igrivom formatu, u "
"kratkim sesijama od pet do deset minuta."

msgid ""
"Reward every correct action immediately — the dog learns faster when the "
"game stays positive and short."
msgstr ""
"Nagrađujte svaku tačnu akciju odmah — pas brže uči kada igra ostane "
"pozitivna i kratka."

msgid "Outdoor and water activities"
msgstr "Aktivnosti na otvorenom i u vodi"

msgid ""
"For active dogs, running, hiking and swimming are excellent sports. "
"Introduce them gradually and consider the breed and age."
msgstr ""
"Za aktivne pse trčanje, planinarenje i plivanje su odlični sportovi. Uvodite"
" ih postepeno i vodite računa o rasi i uzrastu."

msgid ""
"Swimming is a gentle load for the joints, but never leave a dog in the water"
" unattended and check the safety of the reservoir."
msgstr ""
"Plivanje je blag napor za zglobove, ali nikada ne ostavljajte psa bez "
"nadzora u vodi i proverite bezbednost vodenog prostora."

msgid ""
"Avoid intense exercise in extreme heat, especially for brachycephalic breeds"
" with short muzzles."
msgstr ""
"Izbegavajte intenzivne vežbe na velikim vrućinama, posebno za brahicefalne "
"rase sa kratkim njuškama."

msgid "Safety and age limits"
msgstr "Bezbednost i uzrasna ograničenja"

msgid ""
"Puppies' joints and teeth are still forming — choose gentle games and keep "
"the load moderate. Seniors appreciate calmer games: scent tasks, light tug "
"and mental puzzles."
msgstr ""
"Zglobovi i zubi štenaca se još uvek formiraju — birajte nežne igre i držite "
"opterećenje umerenim. Stariji psi više vole smirenije igre: zadatke mirisom,"
" lagano potezanje i mentalne slagalice."

msgid ""
"Watch for signs of fatigue: panting, refusal of the toy, reduced interest. "
"The game should stop while the dog still wants to continue."
msgstr ""
"Pazite na znakove umora: dahtanje, odbijanje igračke, smanjeno "
"interesovanje. Igra treba da se završi dok pas još želi da nastavi."

msgid "If an injury or an unusual condition appears, contact a veterinarian."
msgstr "Ako se pojavi povreda ili neobično stanje, kontaktirajte veterinara."

msgid "Indoor games for bad weather"
msgstr "Igre u zatvorenom za loše vreme"

msgid ""
"A rainy day is no reason to skip exercise. Search games (treats hidden "
"around one room), a short tug session, stair games for healthy dogs (up-and-"
"down retrieves), and trick training all burn energy with almost no space."
msgstr ""
"Kišni dan nije razlog da preskočite aktivnost. Igre traženja (poslastice "
"skrivene po jednoj sobi), kratko povlačenje, igre na stepenicama za zdrave "
"pse (donosenje gore-dole) i učenje trikova troše energiju uz gotovo nikakav "
"prostor."

msgid ""
"Roll a soft ball across the floor, hide a favourite toy under a blanket, or "
"practice «go to your place» with a reward — five to ten minutes of "
"concentrated play indoors can replace a short walk's worth of activity."
msgstr ""
"Svaljajte mekanu loptu po podu, sakrijte omiljenu igračku pod ćebe ili "
"vežbajte «mesto» uz nagradu — pet do deset minuta koncentrisane igre u "
"zatvorenom može zameniti aktivnost kratke šetnje."

msgid "Making your own puzzles"
msgstr "Pravljenje sopstvenih slagalica"

msgid ""
"Simple DIY puzzles: put treats under inverted cardboard cups and move them "
"around; roll kibble into a wrapped towel or a plastic bottle with holes; "
"hide portions in an egg carton with the lids closed. Start easy — the goal "
"is a quick win, not frustration."
msgstr ""
"Jednostavne slagalice uradi sam: stavite poslastice ispod prevrnutih "
"papirnih čašica i pomerajte ih; urolajte granule u umotani peškir ili "
"plastičnu bocu s rupama; sakrijte porcije u kutiji za jaja sa zatvorenim "
"poklopcima. Počnite lako — cilj je brza pobeda, ne frustracija."

msgid ""
"Supervise homemade puzzles and remove them once empty: torn cardboard and "
"plastic caps are fine on the shelf, dangerous in the stomach."
msgstr ""
"Pratite domaće slagalice i uklonite ih čim se isprazne: rastrgani karton i "
"plastični poklopci su bezopasni na polici, opasni u želucu."

msgid "How long and how often"
msgstr "Koliko i koliko često"

msgid ""
"As a rough guide, an adult dog benefits from two active sessions a day — a "
"walk with sniffing and a play session of ten to twenty minutes. Puppies play"
" in short bursts of a few minutes, several times a day; senior dogs prefer "
"one calm session with more searching than running."
msgstr ""
"Kao grubi vodič, odrasli pas ima koristi od dve aktivne sesije dnevno — "
"šetnje s njuškanjem i igranja od deset do dvadeset minuta. Štenci se igraju "
"u kratkim naletima od po nekoliko minuta, nekoliko puta dnevno; stariji psi "
"preferiraju jednu mirnu sesiju s više traženja nego trčanja."

msgid ""
"Watch the dog, not the clock: panting, lying down mid-game, or losing "
"interest are signals to finish. It is always better to stop a little early "
"than to deal with a stiff dog the next morning."
msgstr ""
"Gledajte psa, a ne sat: dahtanje, leganje usred igre ili gubitak "
"interesovanja signali su da se završi. Uvek je bolje stati malo ranije nego "
"se sutra ujutru nositi s ukočenim psom."

msgid "Games with other people and dogs"
msgstr "Igre s drugim ljudima i psima"

msgid ""
"Games with a second person are excellent training material: one calls, the "
"other rewards; or the dog learns to alternate between two people. This "
"builds attention and teaches the dog that both people are equally valuable "
"sources of good things."
msgstr ""
"Igre s drugom osobom odličan su materijal za obuku: jedan zove, drugi "
"nagrađuje; ili pas uči da se menja između dve osobe. To gradi pažnju i uči "
"psa da su obe osobe podjednako vredni izvori lepih stvari."

msgid ""
"With other dogs, choose playmates by matching size and play style, not by "
"age alone. Healthy play includes role reversals, breaks, and loose bodies; "
"if one dog always chases and never gets chased, end the session politely."
msgstr ""
"S drugim psima birajte partnere za igru prema veličini i stilu igre, a ne "
"samo po uzrastu. Zdrava igra uključuje smenu uloga, pauze i opuštena tela; "
"ako jedan pas uvek juri i nikad ne biva juren, završite sesiju uljudno."

msgid ""
"Regular play makes a dog healthier, calmer and happier. Choose games that "
"match your dog's age, energy and taste — and play with joy yourself."
msgstr ""
"Redovna igra čini psa zdravijim, smirenijim i srećnijim. Birajte igre koje "
"odgovaraju uzrastu, energiji i ukusu vašeg psa — i igrajte se sa radošću i "
"sami."

msgid ""
"A variety of games keeps both physical shape and psychological balance."
msgstr ""
"Raznovrsnost igara održava i fizičku kondiciju i psihološku ravnotežu."

msgid "Classification"
msgstr "Klasifikacija"

msgid ""
"We chose the FCI classification as a convenient basis: below are ten groups "
"that bring together breeds of similar origin and purpose. The list is still "
"incomplete — new breeds will be added."
msgstr ""
"Izabrali smo FCI klasifikaciju kao praktičnu osnovu: ispod je deset grupa "
"koje okupljaju rase sličnog porekla i namene. Spisak je za sada nepotpun — "
"nove rase će biti dodavane."

msgid "Learn more"
msgstr "Saznaj"

msgid "Other breeds"
msgstr "Ostale rase"

msgid ""
"Some breeds on the site are not currently placed inside the official FCI "
"classification. They are collected in a separate category so you can still "
"browse and compare them easily."
msgstr ""
"Neke rase na sajtu trenutno nisu smeštene unutar zvanične FCI klasifikacije."
" Sakupljene su u posebnu kategoriju kako biste ih i dalje mogli lako "
"pregledati i upoređivati."

msgid "Oth."
msgstr "Ost."

msgid "Dog guides"
msgstr "Vodiči o psima"

msgid "General information about pet care"
msgstr "Opšte informacije o nezi kućnih ljubimaca"

msgid ""
"The guides contain general information and will help both experienced owners"
" and newcomers learn something new."
msgstr ""
"Vodiči sadrže opšte informacije i pomoći će kako iskusnim vlasnicima, tako i"
" početnicima da saznaju nešto novo."

msgid ""
"Learn how to choose a breed that matches your lifestyle, activity level and "
"living space."
msgstr ""
"Naučite kako da odaberete rasu koja odgovara vašem životnom stilu, nivou "
"aktivnosti i životnom prostoru."

msgid "Read"
msgstr "Pročitaj"

msgid ""
"Learn about early puppy development, socialization, routines and first-life "
"stages."
msgstr ""
"Saznajte više o ranom razvoju šteneta, socijalizaciji, rutinama i prvim "
"fazama života."

msgid ""
"Understand basic training principles, communication and learning "
"consistency."
msgstr "Razumite osnovne principe obuke, komunikaciju i doslednost u učenju."

msgid ""
"Learn about grooming, nutrition, preventive care and general health basics."
msgstr "Saznajte više o nezi, ishrani, preventivnoj nezi i osnovama zdravlja."

msgid ""
"Discover how dogs communicate, express emotions and react to the world "
"around them."
msgstr ""
"Otkrijte kako psi komuniciraju, izražavaju emocije i reaguju na svet oko "
"sebe."

msgid ""
"Daily routines, home adaptation and long-term lifestyle organization with a "
"dog."
msgstr ""
"Svakodnevne rutine, prilagođavanje domu i dugoročna organizacija života sa "
"psom."

msgid ""
"Learn how to choose food, feed by age and build a healthy drinking regime."
msgstr ""
"Naučite kako da odaberete hranu, hranite po uzrastu i uspostavite zdrav "
"režim pijenja."

msgid ""
"Discover safe games and activities that keep your dog active, engaged and "
"happy."
msgstr ""
"Otkrijte bezbedne igre i aktivnosti koje održavaju vašeg psa aktivnim, "
"angažovanim i srećnim."

msgid ""
"Dog health is a combination of prevention, observation, and consistent care."
" It is not only about treating illness, but about maintaining a stable "
"physical condition throughout the dog’s life."
msgstr ""
"Zdravlje psa je kombinacija prevencije, posmatranja i dosledne nege. Ne radi"
" se samo o lečenju bolesti, već o održavanju stabilnog fizičkog stanja tokom"
" celog života psa."

msgid ""
"This guide focuses on general principles of health management, not "
"veterinary diagnosis or treatment. Any medical concerns should always be "
"handled by a qualified veterinarian."
msgstr ""
"Ovaj vodič se fokusira na opšte principe upravljanja zdravljem, a ne na "
"veterinarsku dijagnostiku ili lečenje. Sva medicinska pitanja uvek treba da "
"rešava kvalifikovani veterinar."

msgid "Vaccination"
msgstr "Vakcinacija"

msgid ""
"Health rests on two simple things: everyday care and protection from "
"infections. Vaccination is the second part — and the cheapest insurance a "
"dog can have, because the diseases it prevents are either hard to treat or "
"fatal, especially in puppies."
msgstr ""
"Zdravlje počiva na dve jednostavne stvari: svakodnevnoj nezi i zaštiti od "
"infekcija. Vakcinacija je drugi deo — i najjeftinije osiguranje koje pas "
"može da ima, jer bolesti od kojih štiti teško se leče ili su smrtonosne, "
"posebno kod štenadi."

msgid ""
"Most dogs are vaccinated against rabies, distemper, adenovirus (infectious "
"hepatitis), parvovirus and leptospirosis; in many countries parainfluenza "
"comes in the same combination. Extra vaccines, such as kennel cough or Lyme "
"disease, depend on the region and on whether the dog travels, goes to shows "
"or spends time in the countryside."
msgstr ""
"Većina pasa se vakciniše protiv besnila, štenećaka, adenovirusa (infektivnog"
" hepatitisa), parvovirusa i leptospiroze; u mnogim zemljama parainfluenca je"
" u istoj kombinaciji. Dodatne vakcine — na primer protiv kašlja u "
"odgajivačnicama ili Lajmske bolesti — zavise od regiona i od toga da li pas "
"putuje, ide na izložbe ili provodi vreme na selu."

msgid ""
"There is a schedule, but not one for the whole world: puppies receive a "
"series of injections, adults receive boosters, and the interval depends on "
"the vaccine and on the law of the country — rabies is always fixed by law. "
"Which vaccines and when is decided by your veterinarian; the dates and the "
"product names are written into the international veterinary passport."
msgstr ""
"Raspored postoji, ali nije isti za ceo svet: štenad dobija seriju injekcija,"
" odrasli revakcinaciju, a interval zavisi od vakcine i od zakona zemlje — "
"besnilo je uvek regulisano zakonom. Koje vakcine i kada odlučuje vaš "
"veterinar; datumi i nazivi preparata upisuju se u međunarodni veterinarski "
"pasoš."

msgid ""
"A few practical points: on the day of the visit the dog should be healthy, "
"deworming is done shortly before vaccination, and for a day or two "
"afterwards it is worth skipping bathing, swimming and long journeys. Keep "
"the passport at hand and copy the dates into your own notes or calendar — "
"they are asked for when travelling, in boarding kennels, at shows and at the"
" next visit."
msgstr ""
"Nekoliko praktičnih stvari: na dan posete pas treba da bude zdrav, "
"dehelmintizacija se radi neposredno pre vakcinacije, a dan-dva posle bolje "
"je preskočiti kupanje, plivanje i duga putovanja. Drži pasoš pri ruci i "
"prepiši datume u svoje beleške ili kalendar — traže ih na putovanjima, u "
"pansionima, na izložbama i na sledećem pregledu."

msgid ""
"Vaccination does not replace daily care, and daily care does not replace "
"vaccination: together they are what keeps a dog healthy year after year."
msgstr ""
"Vakcinacija ne zamenjuje svakodnevnu negu, a nega ne zamenjuje vakcinaciju: "
"zajedno drže psa zdravim iz godine u godinu."

msgid "Preventive care and routine checks"
msgstr "Preventivna nega i redovne provere"

msgid ""
"Preventive care is the most important aspect of maintaining long-term "
"health. Regular veterinary check-ups help detect issues early, often before "
"symptoms become visible."
msgstr ""
"Preventivna nega najvažniji je aspekt održavanja dugoročnog zdravlja. "
"Redovne veterinarske provere pomažu da se problemi otkriju rano, često pre "
"nego što simptomi postanu vidljivi."

msgid ""
"Vaccinations, parasite prevention, and routine examinations form the "
"foundation of responsible ownership. These measures reduce the risk of "
"serious illness and improve overall lifespan quality."
msgstr ""
"Vakcinacija, prevencija parazita i rutinski pregledi temelj su odgovornog "
"vlasništva. Ove mere smanjuju rizik od ozbiljnih bolesti i poboljšavaju "
"kvalitet života."

msgid ""
"Many health problems develop gradually, which is why consistent monitoring "
"is more effective than reactive treatment."
msgstr ""
"Mnogi zdravstveni problemi se razvijaju postepeno, zbog čega je dosledno "
"praćenje efikasnije od reaktivnog lečenja."

msgid "Nutrition and physical condition"
msgstr "Ishrana i fizičko stanje"

msgid ""
"Nutrition directly influences energy levels, coat quality, weight, and "
"immune system stability. A balanced diet should be appropriate for the dog’s"
" age, size, and activity level."
msgstr ""
"Ishrana direktno utiče na nivo energije, kvalitet dlake, težinu i stabilnost"
" imunog sistema. Uravnotežena ishrana treba da odgovara uzrastu, veličini i "
"nivou aktivnosti psa."

msgid ""
"Overfeeding is one of the most common health issues in domestic dogs and can"
" lead to obesity-related complications. Underfeeding or low-quality diets "
"can also cause deficiencies and long-term problems."
msgstr ""
"Preterano hranjenje jedan je od najčešćih zdravstvenih problema domaćih pasa"
" i može dovesti do komplikacija povezanih sa gojaznošću. Nedovoljno "
"hranjenje ili ishrana niskog kvaliteta takođe mogu izazvati nedostatke i "
"dugoročne probleme."

msgid ""
"Consistency in feeding habits helps maintain stable digestion and prevents "
"sudden metabolic stress."
msgstr ""
"Doslednost u navikama ishrane pomaže stabilnom varenju i sprečava nagli "
"metabolički stres."

msgid ""
"For practical details — food formats, feeding by age, portions and the "
"drinking regime — see the separate guide on feeding your dog."
msgstr ""
"Za praktične detalje — formate hrane, ishranu po uzrastu, porcije i režim "
"pijenja — pogledajte poseban vodič o ishrani vašeg psa."

msgid "Hygiene and grooming"
msgstr "Higijena i nega dlake"

msgid ""
"Grooming is not only cosmetic but also a health-related necessity. Regular "
"brushing helps prevent skin irritation, removes dead hair, and improves "
"blood circulation."
msgstr ""
"Nega dlake nije samo kozmetika, već i zdravstvena potreba. Redovno češljanje"
" pomaže prevenciji iritacija kože, uklanja mrtvu dlaku i poboljšava "
"cirkulaciju."

msgid ""
"Nail trimming, ear cleaning, and dental care are often overlooked but "
"essential for preventing infections and discomfort."
msgstr ""
"Sečenje noktiju, čišćenje ušiju i nega zuba često se zanemaruju, ali su "
"neophodni za prevenciju infekcija i nelagodnosti."

msgid ""
"The frequency of grooming depends on breed type, coat length, and lifestyle."
msgstr "Učestalost nege zavisi od vrste rase, dužine dlake i životnog stila."

msgid "Common health issues"
msgstr "Česti zdravstveni problemi"

msgid ""
"Some health problems are more common across domestic dogs, including skin "
"allergies, digestive issues, and joint stress in larger breeds."
msgstr ""
"Neki zdravstveni problemi su češći kod domaćih pasa, uključujući alergije na"
" koži, probleme s varenjem i opterećenje zglobova kod većih rasa."

msgid ""
"Early signs often include changes in appetite, energy levels, coat "
"condition, or behavior patterns. These indicators should not be ignored, "
"even if they appear minor."
msgstr ""
"Rani znaci često uključuju promene u apetitu, nivou energije, stanju dlake "
"ili obrascima ponašanja. Ove pokazatelje ne treba ignorisati, čak i ako "
"deluju beznačajno."

msgid ""
"Timely response to early symptoms significantly improves outcomes and "
"reduces long-term complications."
msgstr ""
"Pravovremena reakcija na rane simptome značajno poboljšava ishode i smanjuje"
" dugoročne komplikacije."

msgid "Physical activity and body maintenance"
msgstr "Fizička aktivnost i održavanje tela"

msgid ""
"Regular physical activity supports cardiovascular health, muscle tone, and "
"joint mobility. The required level of activity varies significantly "
"depending on breed and age."
msgstr ""
"Redovna fizička aktivnost podržava kardiovaskularno zdravlje, mišićni tonus "
"i pokretljivost zglobova. Potreban nivo aktivnosti značajno se razlikuje u "
"zavisnosti od rase i uzrasta."

msgid ""
"Insufficient movement can lead to weight gain and reduced overall vitality, "
"while excessive strain without proper rest can cause injuries."
msgstr ""
"Nedovoljno kretanje može dovesti do povećanja telesne težine i smanjene "
"vitalnosti, dok prekomerno opterećenje bez dovoljno odmora može izazvati "
"povrede."

msgid ""
"A balanced approach to exercise is essential for long-term physical "
"stability."
msgstr ""
"Uravnotežen pristup vežbanju neophodan je za dugoročnu fizičku stabilnost."

msgid "Mental health and well-being"
msgstr "Mentalno zdravlje i dobrostanje"

msgid ""
"Mental health is closely linked to physical health in dogs. Stress, boredom,"
" and lack of stimulation can negatively affect the immune system and "
"behavior."
msgstr ""
"Mentalno zdravlje kod pasa je usko povezano sa fizičkim. Stres, dosada i "
"nedostatak stimulacije mogu negativno uticati na imuni sistem i ponašanje."

msgid ""
"Environmental stability, interaction, and predictable routines help maintain"
" emotional balance."
msgstr ""
"Stabilnost okruženja, interakcija i predvidljive rutine pomažu održavanju "
"emotivne ravnoteže."

msgid ""
"A mentally healthy dog is generally more stable, responsive, and physically "
"resilient."
msgstr ""
"Mentalno zdrav pas je generalno stabilniji, prisebniji i fizički otporniji."

msgid "Your dog's health record"
msgstr "Zdravstveni dosije vašeg psa"

msgid ""
"Keep one folder — paper or digital — with everything in it: vaccination "
"dates, deworming and parasite treatment history, microchip number, insurance"
" policy, past test results, and a list of medications with dates. Add your "
"dog's weight at each check-up."
msgstr ""
"Držite jednu fasciklu — papirnu ili digitalnu — sa svime: datumima "
"vakcinacija, istorijom odcrvljivanja i tretmana protiv parazita, brojem "
"mikročipa, polisom osiguranja, ranijim rezultatima analiza i spiskom lekova "
"s datumima. Dodajte težinu psa na svakom pregledu."

msgid ""
"This record saves time in emergencies, makes changing clinics painless, and "
"helps you notice slow trends — for example, gradual weight gain or "
"increasing thirst — long before they become problems."
msgstr ""
"Ovaj zapis štedi vreme u hitnim slučajevima, čini promenu klinike bezbolnom "
"i pomaže da primetite spore trendove — na primer, postepeno debljanje ili "
"povećanu žeđ — daleko pre nego što postanu problemi."

msgid "Dental care in practice"
msgstr "Nega zuba u praksi"

msgid ""
"Brushing two to three times a week with a dog-specific toothpaste is the "
"gold standard. Introduce it gradually: let the dog taste the paste from your"
" finger first, then touch the teeth and gums for a second, and build up to a"
" full session over two to three weeks."
msgstr ""
"Četkanje dva do tri puta nedeljno psećom pastom za zube zlatni je standard. "
"Uvedite ga postepeno: pustite psa da prvo poliže pastu s vašeg prsta, zatim "
"na sekund dodirnite zube i desni i tokom dve do tri nedelje dođite do pune "
"sesije."

msgid ""
"Never use human toothpaste — fluoride and foaming agents are not meant to be"
" swallowed. Dental chews and additives can support the routine but do not "
"replace brushing. Bad breath, yellow-brown tartar, or bleeding gums are "
"reasons for a veterinary dental check."
msgstr ""
"Nikad ne koristite ljudsku pastu za zube — fluor i sredstva za penjenje nisu"
" namenjeni za gutanje. Dentalni zalogaji i dodaci mogu podržati rutinu, ali "
"ne zamenjuju četkanje. Loš zadah, žuto-smeđi kamenac ili krvave desni razlog"
" su za veterinarski pregled zuba."

msgid "Ears, eyes, paws and nails"
msgstr "Uši, oči, šape i nokti"

msgid ""
"Check ears weekly: they should be pale pink inside, without dark buildup or "
"a sour smell. Floppy-eared breeds need this check especially often. Clean "
"with a vet-approved ear solution on a cotton pad — never cotton sticks "
"inside the canal."
msgstr ""
"Proveravajte uši nedeljno: iznutra treba da budu bledo roze, bez tamnih "
"naslaga ili kiselog mirisa. Rase s visećim ušima posebno često trebaju ovu "
"proveru. Čistite rastvorom za uši odobrenim od veterinara na vatom pamučnom "
"jastučiću — nikad štapiće za uši unutar kanala."

msgid ""
"Eyes should be clear and free of crusts; wipe the corners daily with a damp "
"cloth if discharge appears. Nails are due when they touch the floor standing"
" on a hard surface — long nails change the dog's gait and strain the joints "
"over time."
msgstr ""
"Oči treba da budu bistre i bez krasti; ako se pojavi sekret, uglove brišite "
"dnevno vlažnom krpom. Nokti su za rezanje kad dodiruju pod dok pas stoji na "
"tvrdoj površini — dugi nokti menjaju hod psa i opterećuju zglobove vremenom."

msgid ""
"Between the toes, check after every walk for burrs, ice clumps in winter, or"
" salt residue. Trim the hair between paw pads in long-haired breeds to "
"prevent slipping on smooth floors."
msgstr ""
"Između prstiju proveravajte posle svake šetnje da nema čkalja, ledenih "
"grudvi zimi ili ostataka soli. Kod dugodlakih rase skratite dlaku između "
"jastučića da se šape ne bi klizale po glatkom podu."

msgid "Parasite prevention"
msgstr "Prevencija parazita"

msgid ""
"Fleas, ticks, and intestinal worms are prevented with regular products — "
"spot-ons, tablets, or collars — prescribed by a veterinarian based on the "
"dog's weight and lifestyle. Missed doses are the most common reason for "
"breakouts."
msgstr ""
"Buve, krpelji i crevni crvi sprečavaju se redovnim sredstvima — spot-on "
"preparatima, tabletama ili ogrlicama — koje veterinar propisuje prema težini"
" i načinu života psa. Preskočene doze najčešći su razlog pojave."

msgid ""
"After walks in tall grass or woodland, run your hands over the dog's body: "
"armpits, neck, groin, and ears are the favourite attachment sites. Remove a "
"tick with a special tick tool or fine tweezers by twisting gently, then "
"disinfect the spot and monitor the skin for a few days."
msgstr ""
"Posle šetnje u visokoj travi ili šumi pređite rukama po telu psa: pazuh, "
"vrat, prepona i uši omiljena su mesta za krpelje. Uklonite krpelja posebnim "
"alatom ili pincetom nežnim okretanjem, zatim dezinfikujte mesto i pratite "
"kožu nekoliko dana."

msgid "Monitoring weight and body condition"
msgstr "Praćenje težine i kondicije tela"

msgid ""
"The simplest method is a monthly hands-on check. You should feel the ribs "
"easily with light pressure but not see them. Viewed from above, the dog "
"should have a visible waist tuck behind the ribs; from the side, the belly "
"should slope upward."
msgstr ""
"Najjednostavniji metod je mesečna provera rukama. Rebra treba da se lako "
"napipaju uz blag pritisak, ali ne i da se vide. Odozgo pas treba da ima "
"vidljiv struk iza rebara; sa strane stomak treba da se uzdiže nagore."

msgid ""
"Weigh large and giant breeds monthly and small breeds at every vet visit. If"
" the ribs become hard to feel, reduce the daily ration slightly and add more"
" sniffing-based activity; if the ribs show clearly, increase food and check "
"for parasites or other causes."
msgstr ""
"Vagajte velike i ogromne rase mesečno, a male na svakoj poseti veterinaru. "
"Ako rebra postanu teško napipljiva, blago smanjite dnevnu raciju i dodajte "
"više aktivnosti zasnovanih na njuškanju; ako se rebra jasno vide, povećajte "
"hranu i proverite parazite ili druge uzroke."

msgid "When to contact a vet urgently"
msgstr "Kada hitno kontaktirati veterinara"

msgid ""
"Do not wait for a morning appointment if you notice: repeated vomiting or "
"diarrhoea within hours, a visibly bloated and tense abdomen especially in "
"large deep-chested breeds, collapse or extreme weakness, difficulty "
"breathing, sudden severe pain or screaming when touched, bloating of the "
"abdomen with unproductive retching, a seizure lasting more than a minute, or"
" inability to urinate in a male dog."
msgstr ""
"Ne čekajte jutarnji termin ako primetite: ponovljeno povraćanje ili proliv u"
" roku od nekoliko sati, vidljivo nadut i napet stomak naročito kod velikih "
"rasa s dubokim grudima, kolaps ili ekstremnu slabost, otežano disanje, "
"iznenadno jako bola ili cvilenje pri dodiru, nadutost stomaka s neuspešnim "
"povraćanjem, napad koji traje duže od minut ili nemogućnost mokrenja kod "
"mužjaka."

msgid ""
"Also urgent: ingestion of a known poison (chocolate, grapes, xylitol, "
"medications), eye injuries, limping that lasts more than a day, giving birth"
" that stalls for more than an hour between puppies, or any bleeding that "
"does not stop with light pressure."
msgstr ""
"Takođe hitno: unošenje poznatog otrova (čokolada, grožđe, ksilitol, lekovi),"
" povrede oka, šepanje koje traje duže od jednog dana, porođaj koji staje na "
"više od sat vremena između štenaca ili bilo koje krvarenje koje ne staje uz "
"blag pritisak."

msgid "First-aid basics at home"
msgstr "Osnove prve pomoći kod kuće"

msgid ""
"A simple home kit saves valuable minutes: gauze pads and bandage, veterinary"
" disinfectant, tweezers and a tick tool, a digital thermometer, saline "
"solution, and your clinic's number saved in your phone. Learn how to measure"
" temperature and how to bandage a paw before you need it."
msgstr ""
"Jednostavan kućni pribor štedi dragocene minute: gaze i zavoj, veterinarski "
"dezinfikacioni sredstvo, pinceta i alat za krpelje, digitalni termometar, "
"fiziološki rastvor i broj vaše klinike sačuvan u telefonu. Naučite da merite"
" temperaturu i da zavijete šapu pre nego što vam zatreba."

msgid ""
"In case of poisoning, do not induce vomiting on your own — bring the "
"packaging or a sample of the substance to the vet. In case of burns, cool "
"the area with running water and cover it loosely. For heavy bleeding, press "
"a clean pad firmly for several minutes without checking constantly."
msgstr ""
"U slučaju trovanja nemojte sami izazivati povraćanje — donesite pakovanje "
"ili uzorak supstance veterinaru. U slučaju opekotina, ohladite mesto pod "
"mlazom vode i labavo prekrijte. Kod jakog krvarenja čvrsto pritisnite čistu "
"gazu nekoliko minuta bez stalnog proveravanja."

msgid "Heat and cold safety"
msgstr "Bezbednost na vrućini i hladnoći"

msgid ""
"In summer, walk in the early morning and evening; test the pavement with the"
" back of your hand for seven seconds — if it is too hot for your hand, it is"
" too hot for the paws. Never leave a dog in a parked car: even a mild "
"outside temperature quickly becomes fatal inside."
msgstr ""
"Leti šetajte rano ujutru i uveče; testirajte asfalt zadnjom stranom ruke "
"sedam sekundi — ako je vašoj ruci prevruće, prevruće je i za šape. Nikad ne "
"ostavljajte psa u parkiranom automobilu: čak i umerena spoljna temperatura "
"brzo postaje fatalna unutra."

msgid ""
"Signs of overheating are heavy panting, salivation, weakness, and vomiting —"
" move the dog into shade or air conditioning, cool with cool (not ice-cold) "
"water, and contact a vet. In cold weather, short-haired and small dogs "
"benefit from a well-fitting coat; wipe paws after walks to remove road salt."
msgstr ""
"Znaci pregrevanja su jako dahtanje, slinjenje, slabost i povraćanje — "
"odvedite psa u hlad ili klimu, ohladite mlakom (ne ledeno hladnom) vodom i "
"kontaktirajte veterinara. U hladnom vremenu kratkodlakim i malim psima "
"koristi dobro prilagođen kaput; obrišite šape posle šetnje da uklonite so sa"
" puta."

msgid "Senior dog care"
msgstr "Nega starijeg psa"

msgid ""
"Senior dogs benefit from check-ups every six months rather than annually: "
"blood and urine tests catch kidney, liver, and hormonal changes early, while"
" they are still manageable with diet and lifestyle."
msgstr ""
"Stariji psi imaju koristi od pregleda na svakih šest meseci umesto godišnje:"
" analize krvi i urina rano hvataju promene bubrega, jetre i hormona, dok se "
"još mogu držati pod kontrolom ishranom i načinom života."

msgid ""
"At home, add orthopaedic bedding, a non-slip runner on smooth floors, and a "
"ramp for the car or sofa if climbing becomes difficult. Slow walks with "
"plenty of sniffing keep joints and mind in better shape than long demanding "
"marches."
msgstr ""
"Kod kuće dodajte ortopedski ležaj, prostirku protiv klizanja na glatkom podu"
" i rampu za kauč ili auto ako je penjanje postalo teško. Spore šetnje s puno"
" njuškanja drže zglobove i um u boljoj formi od dugih iscrpljujućih marševa."

msgid ""
"Dog health is a continuous process rather than a fixed state. It requires "
"consistent attention to nutrition, hygiene, prevention, and lifestyle "
"balance."
msgstr ""
"Zdravlje psa je neprekidan proces, a ne fiksno stanje. Zahteva doslednu "
"pažnju na ishranu, higijenu, prevenciju i ravnotežu životnog stila."

msgid ""
"When properly managed, these factors significantly increase both the quality"
" and length of a dog’s life."
msgstr ""
"Kada se pravilno vode, ovi faktori značajno povećavaju i kvalitet i dužinu "
"života psa."

msgid "A little mess, a lot of <span class=\"accent-strong\">love</span>"
msgstr "Malo haosa, puno <span class=\"accent-strong\">ljubavi</span>"

msgid "Find by group"
msgstr "Pronađi po grupi"

msgid "Find by breed"
msgstr "Pronađi po rasi"

msgid ""
"Discover the wonderful world of dogs, from playful little companions to "
"loyal adventure buddies, each with a personality of their own."
msgstr ""
"Otkrijte divan svet pasa, od razigranih malih saputnika do vernih drugova u "
"avanturama, svaki sa svojom ličnošću."

msgid "A happy dog"
msgstr "Srećan pas"

msgid "Pause"
msgstr "Pauza"

msgid "Play"
msgstr "Pusti"

msgid "Breed profiles"
msgstr "Profili rasa"

msgid "Explore breeds by size, temperament,<br> lifestyle and more."
msgstr "Istražite rase po veličini, temperamentu,<br> životnom stilu i više."

msgid "Only the best for the best."
msgstr "Samo najbolje za najbolje."

msgid "Four dogs in a garden"
msgstr "Četiri psa u bašti"

msgid "Home"
msgstr "Početna"

msgid "and"
msgstr "i"

msgid "Select breed"
msgstr "Izaberi rasu"

msgid ""
"Please note: these guides are created for informational purposes only, are "
"not medical data and do not replace veterinary advice. If your pet shows "
"signs of health problems — unusual or atypical behavior, refusal to eat, or "
"any other worrying symptoms — please do not self-medicate and take your pet "
"to a veterinarian."
msgstr ""
"Napomena: ovi vodiči su informativnog karaktera, nisu medicinski podaci i ne"
" zamenjuju savet veterinara. Ako vaš ljubimac pokazuje znake zdravstvenih "
"problema — neobično ili netipično ponašanje, odbijanje hrane ili druge "
"zabrinjavajuće simptome — nemojte sami da ga lečite, već ga odvedite "
"veterinaru."

msgid "Contents"
msgstr "Sadržaj"

msgid "Show all contents"
msgstr "Prikaži ceo sadržaj"

msgid "Activity level"
msgstr "Nivo aktivnosti"

msgid "Prey drive"
msgstr "Lovački nagon"

msgid "Where do you live?"
msgstr "Gde živiš?"

msgid "A house with a garden, or it does not matter"
msgstr "U kući sa baštom ili nije bitno"

msgid "An apartment or a small home"
msgstr "U stanu ili manjoj kući"

msgid "How active are you?"
msgstr "Koliko si aktivan?"

msgid "Either is fine"
msgstr "Svejedno je"

msgid "Relaxed, with short walks"
msgstr "Opušteno, sa kratkim šetnjama"

msgid "Active, with long walks and sports"
msgstr "Aktivno, sa dugim šetnjama i sportom"

msgid "Are there children in your home?"
msgstr "Ima li dece u tvom domu?"

msgid "No, or it does not matter"
msgstr "Ne, ili nije bitno"

msgid "Yes, I need a family-friendly dog"
msgstr "Da, treba mi pas pogodan za porodicu"

msgid "Have you trained a dog before?"
msgstr "Jesi li već dresirao psa?"

msgid "Yes, I am experienced"
msgstr "Da, imam iskustva"

msgid "No, this is my first dog"
msgstr "Ne, ovo je moj prvi pas"

msgid "How do you feel about dog hair at home?"
msgstr "Kako gledaš na pseću dlaku u kući?"

msgid "It does not bother me"
msgstr "Ne smeta mi"

msgid "As little as possible"
msgstr "Što manje moguće"

msgid "Do you need a quiet dog?"
msgstr "Treba li ti miran pas?"

msgid "Not really"
msgstr "Ne baš"

msgid "Yes, neighbours are close"
msgstr "Da, komšije su blizu"

msgid "No breed matches all your answers. Try changing one of them."
msgstr "Nijedna rasa ne odgovara svim odgovorima. Pokušaj da promeniš jedan."

msgid "Show matching breeds"
msgstr "Prikaži odgovarajuće rase"

msgid "What «living with a dog» actually means"
msgstr "Šta zapravo znači «život sa psom»"

msgid ""
"Living with a dog is primarily about organizing your daily life around "
"another living being that depends on structure and consistency. It is less "
"about individual tasks like training or feeding, and more about how your "
"home, time, and routines change as a system."
msgstr ""
"Život sa psom prvenstveno znači organizovanje svakodnevnog života oko drugog"
" živog bića koje zavisi od strukture i doslednosti. Manje se radi o "
"pojedinačnim zadacima poput obuke ili ishrane, a više o tome kako se vaš "
"dom, vreme i rutine menjaju kao sistem."

msgid ""
"Once a dog becomes part of the household, your lifestyle stops being fully "
"flexible. Daily planning, free time, and even travel decisions begin to take"
" the dog’s needs into account."
msgstr ""
"Kada pas postane deo domaćinstva, vaš životni stil prestaje da bude potpuno "
"fleksibilan. Svakodnevno planiranje, slobodno vreme, pa i odluke o "
"putovanjima počinju da uzimaju u obzir potrebe psa."

msgid "Daily structure and time organization"
msgstr "Svakodnevna struktura i organizacija vremena"

msgid ""
"A stable daily rhythm is the foundation of life with a dog. Instead of "
"thinking in isolated tasks, it is better to think in blocks of time: "
"morning, midday, evening, and rest periods."
msgstr ""
"Stabilan dnevni ritam temelj je života sa psom. Umesto razmišljanja o "
"izolovanim zadacima, bolje je razmišljati u vremenskim blokovima: jutro, "
"podne, veče i periodi odmora."

msgid ""
"Walks, feeding, and rest are repeated every day at roughly the same times. "
"This creates predictability, which helps the dog feel secure and reduces "
"stress in the household."
msgstr ""
"Šetnje, hranjenje i odmor ponavljaju se svakog dana u približno isto vreme. "
"To stvara predvidljivost koja pomaže psu da se oseća sigurno i smanjuje "
"stres u domaćinstvu."

msgid ""
"The key point is not the exact schedule, but consistency. Dogs adapt well to"
" routine, but poorly to frequent unpredictable changes."
msgstr ""
"Ključna stvar nije tačan raspored, već doslednost. Psi se dobro "
"prilagođavaju rutini, ali loše čestim nepredvidivim promenama."

msgid "Home organization and shared space"
msgstr "Organizacija doma i zajednički prostor"

msgid ""
"Living with a dog also means adapting your physical space. The home becomes "
"a shared environment where both human and dog have defined areas and rules."
msgstr ""
"Život sa psom znači i prilagođavanje fizičkog prostora. Dom postaje "
"zajedničko okruženje u kojem i čovek i pas imaju definisane zone i pravila."

msgid ""
"A resting zone for the dog is important because it creates predictability "
"and reduces overstimulation. At the same time, some areas of the home may "
"need boundaries depending on safety and comfort."
msgstr ""
"Zona odmora za psa je važna jer stvara predvidljivost i smanjuje preteranu "
"stimulaciju. Istovremeno, neki delovi doma mogu zahtevati granice u "
"zavisnosti od bezbednosti i udobnosti."

msgid ""
"This is not about restriction, but about structure. Dogs feel more relaxed "
"when they understand where they can rest, play, or simply observe the "
"environment."
msgstr ""
"To nije ograničavanje, već struktura. Psi se osećaju opuštenije kada "
"razumeju gde mogu da se odmore, igraju ili jednostavno posmatraju okruženje."

msgid "Energy management during the day"
msgstr "Upravljanje energijom tokom dana"

msgid ""
"One of the most important aspects of living with a dog is managing energy "
"levels throughout the day. This does not refer to training, but to balancing"
" activity and rest."
msgstr ""
"Jedan od najvažnijih aspekata života sa psom je upravljanje nivoom energije "
"tokom dana. To se ne odnosi na obuku, već na balansiranje aktivnosti i "
"odmora."

msgid ""
"Without enough physical activity, dogs often become restless. Without enough"
" rest, they can become overstimulated and less predictable in behavior."
msgstr ""
"Bez dovoljno fizičke aktivnosti psi često postaju nemirni. Bez dovoljno "
"odmora mogu postati preterano stimulisani i manje predvidljivi u ponašanju."

msgid ""
"A stable routine naturally balances both: activity during walks and calm "
"periods at home."
msgstr ""
"Stabilna rutina prirodno balansira oboje: aktivnost tokom šetnji i mirne "
"periode kod kuće."

msgid "Time commitment and lifestyle changes"
msgstr "Vremenska posvećenost i promene životnog stila"

msgid ""
"Living with a dog introduces a long-term time commitment that affects daily "
"freedom. Spontaneous decisions such as long trips, late evenings out, or "
"sudden schedule changes become more limited."
msgstr ""
"Život sa psom donosi dugoročnu vremensku posvećenost koja utiče na "
"svakodnevnu slobodu. Spontane odluke poput dugih putovanja, kasnih izlazaka "
"ili naglih promena rasporeda postaju ograničenije."

msgid ""
"This is not a negative aspect, but a structural change in lifestyle. The "
"owner shifts from a fully flexible schedule to a shared routine-based "
"system."
msgstr ""
"To nije negativan aspekt, već strukturna promena životnog stila. Vlasnik "
"prelazi sa potpuno fleksibilnog rasporeda na zajednički sistem zasnovan na "
"rutini."

msgid ""
"Understanding this early helps avoid frustration and unrealistic "
"expectations."
msgstr ""
"Razumevanje ovoga rano pomaže da se izbegnu frustracije i nerealna "
"očekivanja."

msgid "Emotional role in everyday life"
msgstr "Emotivna uloga u svakodnevnom životu"

msgid ""
"Beyond physical routines, dogs also influence emotional structure in the "
"household. Their presence creates continuity, attention cycles, and a sense "
"of shared responsibility."
msgstr ""
"Pored fizičkih rutina, psi utiču i na emotivnu strukturu domaćinstva. "
"Njihovo prisustvo stvara kontinuitet, cikluse pažnje i osećaj zajedničke "
"odgovornosti."

msgid ""
"This does not replace human relationships, but it adds a stable emotional "
"layer to daily life. Many owners experience increased routine stability and "
"reduced isolation."
msgstr ""
"To ne zamenjuje ljudske odnose, ali dodaje stabilan emotivni sloj "
"svakodnevnom životu. Mnogi vlasnici primećuju veću stabilnost rutine i manju"
" izolovanost."

msgid "A sample daily routine"
msgstr "Primer dnevne rutine"

msgid ""
"A realistic day for a healthy adult dog looks like this: a morning walk with"
" toilet and sniffing time, breakfast, a long rest while the household is "
"empty, a midday or evening walk with activity, dinner, quiet time, and a "
"short final walk before bed."
msgstr ""
"Realan dan za zdravog odraslog psa izgleda ovako: jutarnja šetnja s toaletom"
" i vremenom za njuškanje, doručak, dug odmor dok je dom prazan, podnevna ili"
" večernja šetnja s aktivnošću, večera, tiho vreme i kratka finalna šetnja "
"pre spavanja."

msgid ""
"Most of the day an adult dog simply sleeps — this is normal, not boredom. "
"What matters is that the active blocks are predictable and that rest happens"
" in a defined place rather than in the middle of the corridor."
msgstr ""
"Većinu dana odrasli pas jednostavno spava — to je normalno, ne dosada. Ono "
"što je važno je da su aktivni blokovi predvidivi i da odmor bude na "
"definisanom mestu, a ne na sredini hodnika."

msgid "Setting up the dog's zone at home"
msgstr "Uređenje pseće zone kod kuće"

msgid ""
"Every dog needs three fixed points: a resting place it can retreat to, water"
" available around the clock, and a feeding spot that is quiet and rarely "
"passed through. Choose them once and keep them stable — moving the bed every"
" week resets the dog's sense of home."
msgstr ""
"Svaki pas treba tri fiksne tačke: mesto za odmor u koje može da se povuče, "
"vodu dostupnu non-stop i mesto za hranjenje koje je tiho i retko prolazno. "
"Izaberite ih jednom i držite ih stabilno — pomeranje ležaja svake nedelje "
"poništava pasov osećaj doma."

msgid ""
"Decide the no-go areas in advance and keep the rule consistent for all "
"household members. Consistent boundaries reduce tension much more "
"effectively than intermittent permission."
msgstr ""
"Unapred odlučite zabranjene zone i držite pravilo dosledno za sve članove "
"domaćinstva. Dosledne granice mnogo efikasnije smanjuju napetost od "
"povremenih dozvola."

msgid "Working away from home: how long alone"
msgstr "Rad van kuće: koliko dugo sam"

msgid ""
"As a rough guide, an adult healthy dog manages about six to eight hours "
"alone, while puppies need far more frequent breaks — approximately one hour "
"plus one per month of age."
msgstr ""
"Kao grubi vodič, zdrav odrasli pas izdrži oko šest do osam sati sam, dok "
"štenci traže daleko češće pauze — otprilike jedan sat plus jedan za svaki "
"mesec uzrasta."

msgid ""
"If the working day is longer, arrange a midday walk with a neighbour, a dog "
"walker, or daycare — at least several times a week. Long solitary "
"confinement shows up as destructiveness, barking, or house-soiling, and it "
"is a management problem rather than a character flaw."
msgstr ""
"Ako je radni duži, organizujte podnevnu šetnju s komšijom, šetačem pasa ili "
"čuvanjem — barem nekoliko puta nedeljno. Dugo samovanje ispoljava se kao "
"razaranje, ljanje ili nužda u kući, i to je problem organizacije, a ne mana "
"karaktera."

msgid "Travel and transport"
msgstr "Putovanja i transport"

msgid ""
"In the car, the safest option is a secured transport box or a seat-belt "
"harness in the back seat; the front airbag seat is dangerous. Plan a stop "
"every two to three hours on long journeys, offer water, and never leave the "
"dog alone in a parked car in warm weather."
msgstr ""
"U automobilu najbezbednija opcija je obezbeđen transportni boks ili pojas s "
"pojasevom na zadnjem sedištu; prednje sedište s vazdušnim jastukom je "
"opasno. Na dugim putovanjima planirajte pauzu na svaka dva-tri sata, nudite "
"vodu i nikad ne ostavljajte psa samog u parkiranom automobilu na toplom."

msgid ""
"For trips, pack the usual food, bowls, a lead, vaccination records or pet "
"passport, and a familiar blanket. Keeping the feeding schedule unchanged in "
"a new place makes adaptation much easier."
msgstr ""
"Za putovanja spakujte uobičajenu hranu, činije, povodac, evidenciju "
"vakcinacije ili pasoš za kućne ljubimce i poznato ćebe. Nepromenjen raspored"
" hranjenja na novom mestu znatno olakšava navikavanje."

msgid "Guests, deliveries and everyday noise"
msgstr "Gosti, dostave i svakodnevna buka"

msgid ""
"The door is the most exciting and most stressful point in the home. Teach an"
" informal rule: the dog goes to its place when the doorbell rings, rather "
"than rehearsing jumping and barking at every visitor."
msgstr ""
"Vrata su najuzbudljivija i najstresnija tačka u kući. Uvedite neformalno "
"pravilo: pas ide na svoje mesto kad zazvoni zvono, umesto da vežba skakanje "
"i ljanje na svakog posetioca."

msgid ""
"Warn guests in advance not to crowd, stare, or reach over the dog's head; "
"let the animal choose contact. Deliveries, renovations, and parties are "
"predictability breaks — after a noisy day, add calm and rest rather than "
"more activity."
msgstr ""
"Unapred upozorite goste da se ne guraju, ne bulje i ne pružaju ruku preko "
"pseće glave; pustite životinju da sama izabere kontakt. Dostave, renoviranja"
" i žurke su prekidi predvidivosti — posle bučnog dana dodajte mir i odmor, a"
" ne još aktivnosti."

msgid "Cleaning and hair management"
msgstr "Čišćenje i nega dlake"

msgid ""
"Shedding is a daily reality with any dog. A rubber grooming glove, a vacuum "
"with a good filter, and washable covers on the favourite sofa spots remove "
"most of the problem. Brush the dog on the balcony or in the bathroom, not on"
" the carpet."
msgstr ""
"Linjanje je svakodnevna realnost s bilo kojim psom. Gumeni rukav za "
"četkanje, usisivač s dobrim filterom i perive navlake na omiljenim mestima "
"na kauču uklanjaju većinu problema. Četkajte psa na balkonu ili u kupatilu, "
"ne na tepihu."

msgid ""
"Wipe paws after every walk in wet or salty weather, and keep a towel by the "
"door. This two-second habit saves floors, furniture, and the dog's paws."
msgstr ""
"Brišite šape posle svake šetnje u vlažnom ili slanom vremenu i držite peškir"
" kod vrata. Ova dvosekundna navika spašava podove, nameštaj i pseće šape."

msgid "Adding a second dog or pet"
msgstr "Dodavanje drugog psa ili kućnog ljubimca"

msgid ""
"A second animal is not an automatic solution for loneliness. Introduce dogs "
"on neutral territory, keep first meetings short and on lead, and feed them "
"separately. Expect several weeks of parallel living before genuine "
"friendship develops — or accept that it never will."
msgstr ""
"Druga životinja nije automatsko rešenje usamljenosti. Upoznajte pse na "
"neutralnom terenu, držite prve susrete kratke na povodcu i hranite ih "
"odvojeno. Očekujte nekoliko nedelja paralelnog života pre nego se razvije "
"pravo prijateljstvo — ili prihvatite da se nikad neće."

msgid ""
"Before adding a second pet, honestly assess your existing dog's sociability,"
" your time, and your budget — costs roughly double, and veterinary "
"emergencies can coincide."
msgstr ""
"Pre nego što dodate drugog ljubimca, iskreno procenite društvenost svog psa,"
" svoje vreme i budžet — troškovi se otprilike udvostručuju, a veterinarske "
"hitnosti mogu se poklopiti."

msgid ""
"Living with a dog is best understood as organizing a shared life system "
"rather than managing separate tasks. When structure, routine, and space are "
"well balanced, both dog and owner benefit from a stable and predictable "
"environment."
msgstr ""
"Život sa psom najbolje je razumeti kao organizovanje zajedničkog životnog "
"sistema, a ne kao vođenje pojedinačnih zadataka. Kada su struktura, rutina i"
" prostor dobro uravnoteženi, i pas i vlasnik imaju koristi od stabilnog i "
"predvidljivog okruženja."

