msgid "Questions may be sent to the"
msgstr "Pitanja možete poslati preko"

msgid "What training actually is"
msgstr "Šta je zapravo obuka"

msgid ""
"Dog training is the process of building clear communication between human "
"and dog through consistent signals and predictable outcomes. It is not about"
" control, but about establishing shared understanding."
msgstr ""
"Obuka psa je proces izgradnje jasne komunikacije između čoveka i psa kroz "
"dosledne signale i predvidljive ishode. Ne radi se o kontroli, već o "
"uspostavljanju zajedničkog razumevanja."

msgid ""
"Training influences everyday behavior, safety, and the ability of the dog to"
" function comfortably in human environments."
msgstr ""
"Obuka utiče na svakodnevno ponašanje, bezbednost i sposobnost psa da se "
"udobno funkcioniše u ljudskom okruženju."

msgid "Consistency and repetition"
msgstr "Doslednost i ponavljanje"

msgid ""
"Dogs learn through repetition and pattern recognition. The same action must "
"lead to the same result in order for learning to stabilize."
msgstr ""
"Psi uče kroz ponavljanje i prepoznavanje obrazaca. Ista akcija mora dovesti "
"do istog rezultata da bi se učenje stabilizovalo."

msgid ""
"Inconsistent rules create confusion and slow down behavioral development."
msgstr "Nedosledna pravila stvaraju zbunjenost i usporavaju razvoj ponašanja."

msgid ""
"Clear repetition is more effective than complex commands or frequent changes"
" in approach."
msgstr ""
"Jasno ponavljanje efikasnije je od složenih komandi ili čestih promena "
"pristupa."

msgid "Communication signals"
msgstr "Komunikacioni signali"

msgid ""
"Training relies on clear and simple signals that the dog can associate with "
"specific actions. Timing is important because dogs connect behavior and "
"outcome within a short time window."
msgstr ""
"Obuka se oslanja na jasne i jednostavne signale koje pas može povezati sa "
"konkretnim akcijama. Vreme je važno jer psi povezuju ponašanje i ishod u "
"kratkom vremenskom okviru."

msgid ""
"Emotional tone, body language, and predictability of response all influence "
"learning speed."
msgstr ""
"Emotivni ton, govor tela i predvidljivost reakcija utiču na brzinu učenja."

msgid "Common learning mistakes"
msgstr "Česte greške u učenju"

msgid ""
"One of the most common issues is mixing signals, where different responses "
"are given for the same behavior."
msgstr ""
"Jedan od najčešćih problema je mešanje signala, kada se na isto ponašanje "
"daju različite reakcije."

msgid ""
"Another issue is expecting immediate results. Learning takes time and "
"depends on repetition rather than single sessions."
msgstr ""
"Drugi problem je očekivanje trenutnih rezultata. Učenje zahteva vreme i "
"zavisi od ponavljanja, a ne od pojedinačnih sesija."

msgid ""
"Overloading with commands or complexity can slow progress significantly."
msgstr ""
"Preopterećenje komandama ili složenošću može značajno usporiti napredak."

msgid "Building reliable behavior"
msgstr "Izgradnja pouzdanog ponašanja"

msgid ""
"Reliable behavior is achieved through stable routines and predictable "
"outcomes rather than intensity of training."
msgstr ""
"Pouzdano ponašanje postiže se stabilnim rutinama i predvidljivim ishodima, a"
" ne intenzitetom obuke."

msgid ""
"Small, repeated successes build stronger long-term behavior than occasional "
"intensive sessions."
msgstr ""
"Mali, ponovljeni uspesi grade jače dugoročno ponašanje nego povremene "
"intenzivne sesije."

msgid "How a session is structured"
msgstr "Kako je sesija strukturisana"

msgid ""
"One session lasts three to ten minutes depending on the dog's age and "
"concentration. Start with something the dog already knows well, add one "
"small new element, and finish with an easy success and a clear release word."
msgstr ""
"Jedna sesija traje tri do deset minuta u zavisnosti od uzrasta i "
"koncentracije psa. Počnite s nečim što pas već dobro zna, dodajte jedan mali"
" novi element i završite lakim uspehom i jasnom rečju za okončanje."

msgid ""
"Two or three short sessions a day beat one long one. End while the dog still"
" wants to continue — frustration is the fastest way to make training "
"unpleasant."
msgstr ""
"Dve-tri kratke sesije dnevno bolje su od jedne duge. Završite dok pas još "
"želi da nastavi — frustracija je najbrži način da obuka postane neprijatna."

msgid "Markers: how the dog knows it got it right"
msgstr "Marker: kako pas zna da je pogodio"

msgid ""
"A marker — a clicker or a short word like «yes» — tells the dog the exact "
"moment it did the right thing, and predicts a reward that follows. Start by "
"charging the marker: click, then treat, ten to fifteen times in a row, until"
" the dog's ears perk up at the sound."
msgstr ""
"Marker — kliker ili kratka reč poput «bravo» — govori psu tačan moment kada "
"je učinio pravu stvar i najavljuje nadolazeću nagradu. Prvo «napunite» "
"marker: klik, pa poslastica, deset do petnaest puta zaredom, dok se pseće "
"uši ne nakostreše na zvuk."

msgid ""
"Use the marker for behavior you want to see again: the first time the dog "
"lies down on its own, mark it. Timing matters more than enthusiasm — mark "
"while the behavior is happening, not several seconds later."
msgstr ""
"Koristite marker za ponašanje koje želite ponovo da vidite: prvi put kad pas"
" legne sam, označite to. Vreme je važnije od entuzijazma — označite dok se "
"ponašanje dešava, a ne nekoliko sekundi kasnije."

msgid "Choosing the right reward"
msgstr "Odabir prave nagrade"

msgid ""
"Match the reward to the difficulty. At home, ordinary kibble can be the "
"reward; on a street with other dogs, only something exceptional will compete"
" — small pieces of cheese or meat, or a game with a tug toy for dogs that "
"prefer play to food."
msgstr ""
"Prilagodite nagradu težini. Kod kuće obična granula može biti nagrada; na "
"ulici s drugim psima samo se nešto izuzetno može takmičiti — mali komadi "
"sira ili mesa ili igra povlačenja za pse koji više vole igru nego hranu."

msgid ""
"Deliver several rewards in a row for a big success, and one modest reward "
"for an easy repetition. If the dog stops working, the task is too hard or "
"the reward is not valuable enough — change one of the two, not the dog."
msgstr ""
"Dajte nekoliko nagrada zaredom za veliki uspeh, a jednu skromnu za lako "
"ponavljanje. Ako pas prestane da radi, zadatak je previše težak ili nagrada "
"nije dovoljno vredna — promenite jedno od dvoje, ne psa."

msgid "Building a reliable recall"
msgstr "Izgradnja pouzdanog dozivanja"

msgid ""
"The recall is trained on a long lightweight line first, in low-distraction "
"places. Call the dog's name plus one word, and reward every single time it "
"comes — sometimes with a jackpot of several treats and a short game."
msgstr ""
"Dozivanje se prvo vežba na dugoj laganoj uzici, na mestima s malo ometanja. "
"Zovite psa po imenu plus jedna reč i nagradite svaki dolazak — ponekad "
"džekpotom od nekoliko poslastica i kratkom igrom."

msgid ""
"Never punish a dog that came when called, even late or reluctantly. One "
"punishment can undo months of work, because the dog learns that coming to "
"you predicts something unpleasant. If you need the dog close, go and clip "
"the leash on — do not spend the recall word."
msgstr ""
"Nikad ne kažnjavajte psa koji je došao na dozivanje, čak ni kasno ili "
"nevoljno. Jedna kazna može poništiti mesece rada, jer pas uči da dolazak k "
"vama najavljuje nešto neprijatno. Ako vam je pas potreban blizu, priđite i "
"zakačite povodac — ne trošite reč za dozivanje."

msgid "Loose-leash walking"
msgstr "Šetnja s opuštenim povodcem"

msgid ""
"The rule is simple: the leash stays loose, and the dog's position beside you"
" is reinforced with a treat every few steps at first. When the leash "
"tightens, stop and stand still like a tree — moving forward rewards the "
"pulling."
msgstr ""
"Pravilo je jednostavan: povodac ostaje opušten, a položaj psa pored vas se "
"na početku učvršćuje poslasticom svakih nekoliko koraka. Kad se povodac "
"zategne, stanite i ostanite nepomični kao drvo — kretanje unapred nagrađuje "
"vučenje."

msgid ""
"Use a well-fitted harness rather than a collar for daily walks; choose "
"reward placement deliberately: treats are delivered next to your leg, not in"
" front of it, so the dog learns the position that pays."
msgstr ""
"Za svakodnevne šetnje koristite dobro prilagođen pojas umesto ogrlice; mesto"
" nagrade birajte namerno: poslastica se daje pored vaše noge, ne ispred nje,"
" da bi pas naučio položaj koji se isplati."

msgid "Proofing: from the room to the real world"
msgstr "Učvršćivanje: iz sobe u pravi svet"

msgid ""
"Behavior only becomes reliable when it is practiced at increasing difficulty"
" levels: quiet room, then yard, then a calm street, then around "
"distractions. Increase one parameter at a time — distance from the "
"distraction, duration of the stay, or duration of the behavior."
msgstr ""
"Ponašanje postaje pouzdano tek kad se vežba na rastućim nivoima težine: "
"mirna soba, pa dvorište, pa mirna ulica, pa oko ometanja. Povećavajte jedan "
"parametar po put — udaljenost od ometanja, trajanje zadržavanja ili trajanje"
" ponašanja."

msgid ""
"If a behavior falls apart in the real world, it is not a setback — it shows "
"the next training step. Step back one level, succeed there, and move forward"
" again slowly."
msgstr ""
"Ako se ponašanje raspada u pravom svetu, to nije korak unazad — pokazuje "
"sledeći korak obuke. Vratite se jedan nivo unazad, uspejte tamo i ponovo se "
"polako krećite napred."

msgid "Everyday problems that training fixes"
msgstr "Svakodnevni problemi koje obuka rešava"

msgid ""
"Jumping on guests: reward four paws on the floor the moment the dog is calm,"
" and turn away the instant jumping starts. The dog learns that calmness "
"opens the door to attention."
msgstr ""
"Skakanje na goste: nagradite četiri šape na podu u trenutku kad je pas miran"
" i odvrnite se čim skakanje počne. Pas uči da mir otvara vrata pažnji."

msgid ""
"Demand barking: never reward it with attention, including shouting; teach "
"one quiet signal and reward the silence after. Stealing from tables and "
"counters is managed by management first: nothing edible left within reach, "
"one clear rule, and a rewarded alternative place nearby."
msgstr ""
"Ljanje iz zahteva: nikad ga ne nagrađujte pažnjom, uključujući vikanje; "
"naučite jedan tih signal i nagradite nakon tišine. Krađu s stolova i pultova"
" prvo rešava organizacija: ništa jestivo na dohvat ruke, jedno jasno pravilo"
" i nagrađeno alternativno mesto u blizini."

msgid "What not to do"
msgstr "Šta ne treba raditi"

msgid ""
"Avoid punishment after the fact — the dog connects it with whatever is "
"happening now, not with what happened five minutes ago. Avoid physical "
"corrections, shouting, and holding a dog down; they teach avoidance of the "
"owner, not the desired behavior."
msgstr ""
"Izbegavajte kaznu nakon činjenice — pas je povezuje sa onim što se dešava "
"sada, a ne sa onim što je bilo pre pet minuta. Izbegavajte fizičke "
"korekcije, vikanje i držanje psa dole; uče izbegavanje vlasnika, a ne "
"željeno ponašanje."

msgid ""
"Do not teach several commands at once, do not repeat a command endlessly "
"when the dog does not respond — change the situation instead — and do not "
"use the dog's name for corrections, or it will stop predicting anything "
"good."
msgstr ""
"Nemojte učiti nekoliko komandi odjednom, nemojte beskrajno ponavljati "
"komandu ako pas ne reaguje — promenite situaciju umesto toga — i ne "
"koristite psovo ime za korekcije, inače će prestati da najavljuje bilo šta "
"dobro."

msgid ""
"Training is a communication system that develops over time through "
"consistency and clarity. When properly structured, it creates stability and "
"reduces misunderstandings between dog and owner."
msgstr ""
"Obuka je komunikacioni sistem koji se razvija tokom vremena kroz doslednost "
"i jasnoću. Kada je pravilno strukturisana, stvara stabilnost i smanjuje "
"nesporazume između psa i vlasnika."

